{"parentUuid":"40ecb6ea-3bdf-4db3-90de-57b3e467b04b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e762fa25-d21d-450d-8c0d-cd33dba6f7fe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PWYNbRdm6oevq8DeUG3KDw","type":"tool_result","content":"=========== trail 152\nTrail #152: Changelog entries read well for users\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/29          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/152/changes/callisto/29\n    callisto/90          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/152/changes/callisto/90\n    callisto/94          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/152/changes/callisto/94\n\nDescription:\nProblem: the pending 0.17.0 changelog has a double bullet that fuses two fixes, entries that bundle unrelated fixes, vague lead-ins like 'Fixes four mismatches', plain-text identifiers and unexplained internal terms. Callisto accepts any free text as a changeset summary, so nothing catches this before the release PR.\n\nOutcome: every changelog entry is one topic, leads with what the user sees now, and renders cleanly; and Callisto helps authors get there.\n\nDone when: the pending changesets are rewritten one topic per file (the release PR shows clean entries), and we have decided which checks Callisto itself should run on summaries and where the rendered changelog is shown before merge.\n\nWork: the changeset rewrite PR.\n=========== trail 180\nTrail #180: The release PR says why it is held\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH                 STATUS  URL\n    callisto/40                         merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/180/changes/callisto/40\n    callisto/92  feat/release-pr-token  closed  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/180/changes/callisto/92\n\nDescription:\nThe `Hold release PR` workflow drafts the open release PR on every push to `main`, and the refresh marks it ready only when it was built from the current tip. When the refresh fails, the PR stays a draft with no explanation, so a person sees an unmergeable PR and has to find the failed Release run.\n\nPlan: when the hold workflow drafts a PR, add a short comment that names the push that held it and says the Release workflow will mark it ready after a refresh. When the refresh succeeds, mark it ready and edit that comment. When the refresh fails, edit it to link the failed run. One comment, edited in place, never repeated.\n\nAlso confirm in a real release the first time it runs: the draft-and-restore path, `gh pr ready` and `--undo`, which are unverified against GitHub.\n\nDone when a held release PR carries a comment that states why, a failed refresh links its run, and the first real release shows the full draft-then-ready cycle.\n=========== trail 247\nTrail #247: The release pipeline runs verification alongside planning and building\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/71          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/247/changes/callisto/71\n\nDescription:\nVerify sat in front of plan and build though only publishing needs it. Splitting out a gate job saves about six minutes of a 32 minute release. Draft until 0.18.0 is released and its timings are read.\n=========== trail 246\nTrail #246: A configured registry destination is honored or refused\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/68          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/246/changes/callisto/68\n\nDescription:\nA cargo registry url and a yarn npm registry were accepted from callisto.toml and then dropped, so a release could publish to a different registry than configured. Found by the 2026-11 sweeps and reproduced on the real binary.\n=========== trail 245\nTrail #245: Version writes keep what they should\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/66          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/245/changes/callisto/66\n\nDescription:\ncallisto version dropped a root manifest BOM and CRLF, skipped a changelog entry when a heading was merely quoted, left two titles after a rename and rewrote npm override references. Found by the 2026-11 sweeps, each reproduced before the fix.\n=========== trail 233\nTrail #233: Generated release workflows run in a downstream repo\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/55          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/233/changes/callisto/55\n    callisto/56          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/233/changes/callisto/56\n    callisto/57          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/233/changes/callisto/57\n    callisto/60          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/233/changes/callisto/60\n\nDescription:\nThe generated matrix workflow checked out the branch, leaving HEAD attached, so release plan/execute/build-python stopped with E170. Also covers the attestation flags, template pin drift and other generated-output gaps found by the 2026-11 sweeps.\n=========== trail 237\nTrail #237: Cleanup: dead code, stale docs and narration\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/61          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/61\n    callisto/62          closed  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/62\n    callisto/63          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/63\n    callisto/64          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/64\n    callisto/65          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/65\n    callisto/70          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/70\n\nDescription:\nRemoves code, error codes and files nothing uses; fixes docs and specs that no longer match the code; replaces history-style comments with present-tense ones; adds a CI guard so they do not return. Findings come from the 2026-11 dead-code and narration sweeps.\n=========== trail 162\nTrail #162: A stale release PR can no longer wedge releases\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/32          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/162/changes/callisto/32\n    callisto/34          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/162/changes/callisto/34\n\nDescription:\nEvery push to `main` since 2026-11-02 18:07Z fails the Release workflow at \"Derive and hash intent\" with `E165: no changeset was consumed by this commit`. Nothing was published: no `0.17.0` tag, GitHub release or crates.io version exists, and the latest is `0.16.0`.\n\nWhat happened. Release PR #409 was built from eight generated-name changesets (`gentle-tigers-leap.md` and others). #420 (merged 16:49Z) deleted those eight and added topic-named ones. The release workflow should have refreshed #409 on that push, but its \"Create or update the Callisto release PR\" step failed at 16:57:39Z with `gh: Something went wrong while executing your query` (GitHub request ID 2445:25D0C1:8E695E:1D11C81:6AE8C100), right after printing the 0.17.0 version plan. #409 stayed stale and was merged at 18:07Z. Its eight deletions were already on `main`, so the merge deleted nothing, left every topic changeset pending, and still applied the `0.17.0` bumps, changelogs and `release-decision.json`. The release commit consumed no changesets, and every later push retries it and fails the same way.\n\nCause, in layers. The trigger was a transient GitHub GraphQL error. `create-or-update-release-pr.sh` has no retry on its forge calls (`gh pr list`, the `createCommitOnBranch` mutation, the ref moves, `gh pr edit`), only on the final verify loop, and the workflow runs only on pushes to `main`, so one failed refresh leaves the release PR stale until the next push. Nothing stops a stale release PR from merging: E165 is only raised after the merge, and recovery is a manual revert.\n\nWhich `gh` call failed is not known: the script suppresses stderr on some calls, and the log shows only the final message.\n\nPlan.\n1. Revert the release payload of the #409 merge (PR #423) so the next push regenerates the release PR. Verify the Release workflow turns green and the new release PR consumes every pending changeset.\n2. Retry the forge calls in `create-or-update-release-pr.sh` with bounded backoff, and stop swallowing stderr, so one 5xx does not strand the release PR.\n3. Add a pre-merge guard: a check on the release PR that fails when the merge result still has pending changesets, or when the PR was built from a changeset set that differs from `main`. Specify first, then test, in the release-PR specs.\n4. Write down the E165 recovery (revert the release payload) in the release docs, and decide whether `callisto release pending` should name it.\n5. Separate: `callisto status` warns `tag candidate callisto-graph@0 matched glob but placeholder 0 is not a valid SemVer version`, which suggests stray tags.\n\nDone when the Release workflow is green on `main`, a regenerated release PR consumes the pending changesets, and the retry and guard exist with tests.\n=========== trail 176\nTrail #176: Release previews and preconditions work as specified\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/37          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/176/changes/callisto/37\n    callisto/45          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/176/changes/callisto/45\n\nDescription:\nFour bugs found by the 2026-11-02 spec re-check, all in the release command's error and preview paths. Each is a spec criterion the code does not meet.\n\n1. `callisto release --dry-run` fails with E170 (\"requires a GitHub remote\") in a workspace with a `[[release.artifact]]` and no `origin`, because `prepare_remote` demands a remote even for a preview (`derive.rs:317-323`). REL-CMD-04 and REL-CMD-05 say a preview performs no effect, works without `origin`, and prints one note. Fix: in preview, leave upload and forge operations unbound and print the note.\n2. `release plan --from-release-commit` fails with E164 on a shallow clone and with E224 or E164 on a SHA-256 repository, because it parses the commit before the repository trust check. REL-AUTH-05 says every route fails with E266 (shallow) or E265 (not SHA-1). Fix: run the trust check first. No test asserts E265 or E266.\n3. `release plan --package X --artifact-repository o/r` without `--orchestration-revision` is a clap usage error (exit 2, no E-code), because `cli.rs:360` declares `requires`. REL-AUTH-08 says a source without `[release]` ignores both flags and one with it fails with E231. Fix: drop the `requires` so the handler decides.\n4. With an unreachable `origin`, `callisto release --dry-run` prints the version-control tool's fatal message to stderr, because the origin tag probe uses `run_with_timeout`, which echoes the child's stderr (`local.rs:123`). REL-RERUN-08 says nothing is printed. Fix: use the quiet runner and add an end-to-end test for an unreadable remote.\n\nDone when each has a test that fails before the fix and passes after, the specs are unchanged (the code matches them), and the release command's E-codes match `docs/errors.md`.\n=========== trail 179\nTrail #179: Packages and fixed groups appear and release the way they are configured\n  Status:    open\n\nDescription:\nTwo open DX gaps from the plan. Both change core behavior the plan left to the owner, so this trail holds the verified facts and a recommendation; nothing is built yet.\n\n1. Private workspace root listed as a package. Verified with the built binary on 2026-11-02: a root `package.json` that is `private`, has `workspaces`, a name and a version is listed (`npm/monorepo 0.0.0` in `status`), and `[[package]] match = \"npm/monorepo\"` with `publish-to = [\"none\"]` does not hide it. A private root with no version is already dropped (WS-DISC-08). Options: (A) drop any private root that has `workspaces` by default: simple, but a root that is deliberately versioned (a product or repository version) would silently vanish, and the spec admits a named root always; (B) an explicit `ignore = true` on `[[package]]` and `[[package-set]]`: no behavior change for anyone, one new key; (C) document `publish-to = [\"none\"]` as the answer: the package stays listed. Recommendation: B. Semantics to specify first: the package is removed from the graph after discovery; a changeset or g\n\n2. E194, several packages sharing a `v{version}` tag. It is an `init`-time error, raised when a repository migrates from a single shared tag (the Changesets fixed-group style). Today the answer is a per-package `tag-template` plus `previous-tag-templates`, which works but gives up the single tag and single GitHub release a fixed group had. Giving a group one tag and one release means choosing the owner package, the ordering of the registry publishes against that tag, and the title, which is exactly the \"shared tag and forge ordering\" ADR 12 covers. ADR 12 is still Proposed. Recommendation: accept or revise ADR 12 first, then design the group tag on top of it; the release title alone is the cheap part and can follow.\n\nDecisions needed from the owner: B for the private root (yes or no), and whether to accept ADR 12 now. With a yes on B I will write the spec text, then the code and tests in one PR.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2759c888-83a2-4adc-bda9-65e04d5b81b5","timestamp":"2026-11-10T15:10:20.751Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=========== trail 152\nTrail #152: Changelog entries read well for users\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/29          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/152/changes/callisto/29\n    callisto/90          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/152/changes/callisto/90\n    callisto/94          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/152/changes/callisto/94\n\nDescription:\nProblem: the pending 0.17.0 changelog has a double bullet that fuses two fixes, entries that bundle unrelated fixes, vague lead-ins like 'Fixes four mismatches', plain-text identifiers and unexplained internal terms. Callisto accepts any free text as a changeset summary, so nothing catches this before the release PR.\n\nOutcome: every changelog entry is one topic, leads with what the user sees now, and renders cleanly; and Callisto helps authors get there.\n\nDone when: the pending changesets are rewritten one topic per file (the release PR shows clean entries), and we have decided which checks Callisto itself should run on summaries and where the rendered changelog is shown before merge.\n\nWork: the changeset rewrite PR.\n=========== trail 180\nTrail #180: The release PR says why it is held\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH                 STATUS  URL\n    callisto/40                         merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/180/changes/callisto/40\n    callisto/92  feat/release-pr-token  closed  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/180/changes/callisto/92\n\nDescription:\nThe `Hold release PR` workflow drafts the open release PR on every push to `main`, and the refresh marks it ready only when it was built from the current tip. When the refresh fails, the PR stays a draft with no explanation, so a person sees an unmergeable PR and has to find the failed Release run.\n\nPlan: when the hold workflow drafts a PR, add a short comment that names the push that held it and says the Release workflow will mark it ready after a refresh. When the refresh succeeds, mark it ready and edit that comment. When the refresh fails, edit it to link the failed run. One comment, edited in place, never repeated.\n\nAlso confirm in a real release the first time it runs: the draft-and-restore path, `gh pr ready` and `--undo`, which are unverified against GitHub.\n\nDone when a held release PR carries a comment that states why, a failed refresh links its run, and the first real release shows the full draft-then-ready cycle.\n=========== trail 247\nTrail #247: The release pipeline runs verification alongside planning and building\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/71          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/247/changes/callisto/71\n\nDescription:\nVerify sat in front of plan and build though only publishing needs it. Splitting out a gate job saves about six minutes of a 32 minute release. Draft until 0.18.0 is released and its timings are read.\n=========== trail 246\nTrail #246: A configured registry destination is honored or refused\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/68          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/246/changes/callisto/68\n\nDescription:\nA cargo registry url and a yarn npm registry were accepted from callisto.toml and then dropped, so a release could publish to a different registry than configured. Found by the 2026-11 sweeps and reproduced on the real binary.\n=========== trail 245\nTrail #245: Version writes keep what they should\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/66          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/245/changes/callisto/66\n\nDescription:\ncallisto version dropped a root manifest BOM and CRLF, skipped a changelog entry when a heading was merely quoted, left two titles after a rename and rewrote npm override references. Found by the 2026-11 sweeps, each reproduced before the fix.\n=========== trail 233\nTrail #233: Generated release workflows run in a downstream repo\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/55          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/233/changes/callisto/55\n    callisto/56          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/233/changes/callisto/56\n    callisto/57          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/233/changes/callisto/57\n    callisto/60          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/233/changes/callisto/60\n\nDescription:\nThe generated matrix workflow checked out the branch, leaving HEAD attached, so release plan/execute/build-python stopped with E170. Also covers the attestation flags, template pin drift and other generated-output gaps found by the 2026-11 sweeps.\n=========== trail 237\nTrail #237: Cleanup: dead code, stale docs and narration\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/61          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/61\n    callisto/62          closed  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/62\n    callisto/63          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/63\n    callisto/64          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/64\n    callisto/65          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/65\n    callisto/70          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/237/changes/callisto/70\n\nDescription:\nRemoves code, error codes and files nothing uses; fixes docs and specs that no longer match the code; replaces history-style comments with present-tense ones; adds a CI guard so they do not return. Findings come from the 2026-11 dead-code and narration sweeps.\n=========== trail 162\nTrail #162: A stale release PR can no longer wedge releases\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/32          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/162/changes/callisto/32\n    callisto/34          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/162/changes/callisto/34\n\nDescription:\nEvery push to `main` since 2026-11-02 18:07Z fails the Release workflow at \"Derive and hash intent\" with `E165: no changeset was consumed by this commit`. Nothing was published: no `0.17.0` tag, GitHub release or crates.io version exists, and the latest is `0.16.0`.\n\nWhat happened. Release PR #409 was built from eight generated-name changesets (`gentle-tigers-leap.md` and others). #420 (merged 16:49Z) deleted those eight and added topic-named ones. The release workflow should have refreshed #409 on that push, but its \"Create or update the Callisto release PR\" step failed at 16:57:39Z with `gh: Something went wrong while executing your query` (GitHub request ID 2445:25D0C1:8E695E:1D11C81:6AE8C100), right after printing the 0.17.0 version plan. #409 stayed stale and was merged at 18:07Z. Its eight deletions were already on `main`, so the merge deleted nothing, left every topic changeset pending, and still applied the `0.17.0` bumps, changelogs and `release-decision.json`. The release commit consumed no changesets, and every later push retries it and fails the same way.\n\nCause, in layers. The trigger was a transient GitHub GraphQL error. `create-or-update-release-pr.sh` has no retry on its forge calls (`gh pr list`, the `createCommitOnBranch` mutation, the ref moves, `gh pr edit`), only on the final verify loop, and the workflow runs only on pushes to `main`, so one failed refresh leaves the release PR stale until the next push. Nothing stops a stale release PR from merging: E165 is only raised after the merge, and recovery is a manual revert.\n\nWhich `gh` call failed is not known: the script suppresses stderr on some calls, and the log shows only the final message.\n\nPlan.\n1. Revert the release payload of the #409 merge (PR #423) so the next push regenerates the release PR. Verify the Release workflow turns green and the new release PR consumes every pending changeset.\n2. Retry the forge calls in `create-or-update-release-pr.sh` with bounded backoff, and stop swallowing stderr, so one 5xx does not strand the release PR.\n3. Add a pre-merge guard: a check on the release PR that fails when the merge result still has pending changesets, or when the PR was built from a changeset set that differs from `main`. Specify first, then test, in the release-PR specs.\n4. Write down the E165 recovery (revert the release payload) in the release docs, and decide whether `callisto release pending` should name it.\n5. Separate: `callisto status` warns `tag candidate callisto-graph@0 matched glob but placeholder 0 is not a valid SemVer version`, which suggests stray tags.\n\nDone when the Release workflow is green on `main`, a regenerated release PR consumes the pending changesets, and the retry and guard exist with tests.\n=========== trail 176\nTrail #176: Release previews and preconditions work as specified\n  Status:    open\n  Changes:\n    CHANGE       BRANCH  STATUS  URL\n    callisto/37          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/176/changes/callisto/37\n    callisto/45          merged  https://entire.com/gh/orin-dx/-/trails/176/changes/callisto/45\n\nDescription:\nFour bugs found by the 2026-11-02 spec re-check, all in the release command's error and preview paths. Each is a spec criterion the code does not meet.\n\n1. `callisto release --dry-run` fails with E170 (\"requires a GitHub remote\") in a workspace with a `[[release.artifact]]` and no `origin`, because `prepare_remote` demands a remote even for a preview (`derive.rs:317-323`). REL-CMD-04 and REL-CMD-05 say a preview performs no effect, works without `origin`, and prints one note. Fix: in preview, leave upload and forge operations unbound and print the note.\n2. `release plan --from-release-commit` fails with E164 on a shallow clone and with E224 or E164 on a SHA-256 repository, because it parses the commit before the repository trust check. REL-AUTH-05 says every route fails with E266 (shallow) or E265 (not SHA-1). Fix: run the trust check first. No test asserts E265 or E266.\n3. `release plan --package X --artifact-repository o/r` without `--orchestration-revision` is a clap usage error (exit 2, no E-code), because `cli.rs:360` declares `requires`. REL-AUTH-08 says a source without `[release]` ignores both flags and one with it fails with E231. Fix: drop the `requires` so the handler decides.\n4. With an unreachable `origin`, `callisto release --dry-run` prints the version-control tool's fatal message to stderr, because the origin tag probe uses `run_with_timeout`, which echoes the child's stderr (`local.rs:123`). REL-RERUN-08 says nothing is printed. Fix: use the quiet runner and add an end-to-end test for an unreadable remote.\n\nDone when each has a test that fails before the fix and passes after, the specs are unchanged (the code matches them), and the release command's E-codes match `docs/errors.md`.\n=========== trail 179\nTrail #179: Packages and fixed groups appear and release the way they are configured\n  Status:    open\n\nDescription:\nTwo open DX gaps from the plan. Both change core behavior the plan left to the owner, so this trail holds the verified facts and a recommendation; nothing is built yet.\n\n1. Private workspace root listed as a package. Verified with the built binary on 2026-11-02: a root `package.json` that is `private`, has `workspaces`, a name and a version is listed (`npm/monorepo 0.0.0` in `status`), and `[[package]] match = \"npm/monorepo\"` with `publish-to = [\"none\"]` does not hide it. A private root with no version is already dropped (WS-DISC-08). Options: (A) drop any private root that has `workspaces` by default: simple, but a root that is deliberately versioned (a product or repository version) would silently vanish, and the spec admits a named root always; (B) an explicit `ignore = true` on `[[package]]` and `[[package-set]]`: no behavior change for anyone, one new key; (C) document `publish-to = [\"none\"]` as the answer: the package stays listed. Recommendation: B. Semantics to specify first: the package is removed from the graph after discovery; a changeset or g\n\n2. E194, several packages sharing a `v{version}` tag. It is an `init`-time error, raised when a repository migrates from a single shared tag (the Changesets fixed-group style). Today the answer is a per-package `tag-template` plus `previous-tag-templates`, which works but gives up the single tag and single GitHub release a fixed group had. Giving a group one tag and one release means choosing the owner package, the ordering of the registry publishes against that tag, and the title, which is exactly the \"shared tag and forge ordering\" ADR 12 covers. ADR 12 is still Proposed. Recommendation: accept or revise ADR 12 first, then design the group tag on top of it; the release title alone is the cheap part and can follow.\n\nDecisions needed from the owner: B for the private root (yes or no), and whether to accept ADR 12 now. With a yes on B I will write the spec text, then the code and tests in one PR.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6dbcd1e1-d94d-451a-bba8-a750b9e707d5","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","branch":"fix/unreleased-needs-a-tag","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/unreleased-needs-tag","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"40ecb6ea-3bdf-4db3-90de-57b3e467b04b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8"