es with no publish target, as an OPTIONAL field with `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = ...)]` so existing preview files still load and `RELEASE_PREVIEW_SCHEMA_VERSION` stays the same. Add a test that an old preview JSON without the field still deserializes.\n2. `publish_outlook_in` fills it. Keep the selection and planning in that one function.\n3. `publish_section` renders one line after the publish table when the list is non-empty: `Versioned, not published: \\`callisto-fixtures\\` (no publish target).` Several names are comma-separated and each in backticks. Nothing is rendered when the list is empty. Follow the surrounding rendering style and the repo's emoji conventions (do not add new emoji; existing ones in the PR body are settled).\n4. The case where no bumped package publishes anywhere (currently an empty Planned plan): the line still appears, naming the versioned-only packages.\n5. Tests first (fail before, pass after): extend the existing end-to-end test `a_private_fixed_group_member_does_not_make_the_publish_plan_fail` in crates/callisto-cli/tests/emit_preview_tests.rs (or add a sibling) to assert the private member appears in the new field, and add a render test in pr_body.rs for the line (with names, with none).\n6. Update docs/architecture/versioning.md (the ReleasePreview bullet) and the relevant criterion in docs/specs/release.json (REL-PR-10 describes the publish section; keep valid JSON).\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new flags or config. Match surrounding comment density; one short line only for a non-obvious why. Do NOT add a changeset file; instead return, in plain words, what a user now sees and why it helps.\n\nVerify: `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, each judged by exit code. Mutation check: stop filling the field and confirm the new tests fail, then restore. Do NOT commit, push, or sign; leave changes uncommitted in your worktree. Final report: files changed, new test names,