{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytxL4nYq1T7cJBdRjiu","lastSequenceNum":8710,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"c211518ecd72f9d545d8713f08b410a6d449fc23a7ed1509d45702e7eb6f3481","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013hmsM7PzbYYUqHaNUw4pLb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a66cc14c58c4599d3/.changeset/skip-private-workspace-root.md","content":"---\ncallisto-cli: minor\n---\n\nA private npm workspace root is no longer treated as a package.\n\n- A root `package.json` that is `private` and lists `workspaces` is skipped, so it stops appearing in `status` and in release plans. Many project templates give that root a version such as `0.0.0`, and until now Callisto listed it as a package even though it only holds scripts and tooling, is never published, and nothing depends on it by version.\n- `status` prints one line when it skips a root, so it never disappears silently.\n- To version the root anyway, add a `[[package]]` block to `callisto.toml` with `match = \"npm/<name>\"`, where `<name>` is the root's `package.json` name, such as `match = \"npm/monorepo\"`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CSc9cYJc884paocfmKMyLR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -S -q -m \"docs: explain why a private root has a version and how to name it\" && git push -q 2>&1 | tail -1; git log -1 --format=%h","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true,"timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011CuZHBEkuf4CfN76qjn5v4","name":"EnterWorktree","input":{"path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a68476f02ef165c79"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
