{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"1e23c08c535f1d703cda782978edc1197145394148758a891b4cc6e3505bf583","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FYV6BSX8vzCuU1JZ52vh9v","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr494_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\n`changed_source_files_since_last_tag` ran one `git diff` per package. That made `version --emit-preview` scale linearly with package count, against the AGENTS.md rule of no git process per package. It now runs one diff per distinct last-tag commit and attributes each path to every package whose directory contains it, nested directories included. Untagged or directory-less packages still use one call each. Pathspecs split across several diffs past 24,000 bytes to stay under the Windows 32 KB command-line limit.\n\nWith 150 changed packages tagged at one commit, a synthetic workspace went from 151 diffs and 3.8 s to 4 diffs and 1.0 s.\n\n## Verify\n\nNew tests count git calls and compare the batched result with a per-package reference (root package, nested and spaced directories, untagged package, ignored paths, staged file). A small-budget test shows chunking changes nothing. Forcing per-package diffs or ignoring the budget fails these tests. `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI not run.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dk8EMsFo6BvJFmH7LJ6jQj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 494 --title \"perf(graph): list changed files with one git diff per tag commit\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr494_final.md; gh pr checks 490 2>&1 | grep -E \"macos-arm64\"; gh pr checks 487 2>&1 | grep -E \"macos-arm64\"","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
