{"parentUuid":"225d2385-91e6-4c2b-8621-f940d114b46f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgupf27J7X9ucivRjTdHt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gr6G7dz8i92nRpHWdQZCr7","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr503-body","description":"PR body for 503","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr503.diff. Five small consistency fixes from a pre-1.0 audit of docs/stability.md. (1) `callisto add --package cargo/a:patch --package cargo/a:major` wrote both lines into one changeset, which Callisto's own reader then rejected (`status --check` exited 1); `add` now fails with new code E329 (\"package listed more than once in --package\"), writes nothing, and catches bare and qualified spellings of the same package; the interactive wizard cannot produce duplicates. (2) `--strict` help was wrong for `snapshot` (\"Abort if the workspace graph contains error-severity diagnostics\": graph errors abort with or without the flag) and incomplete for `version`; both now say what the flag does. (3) `status --format json` printed `lastReleasedVersion: null` but omitted `lastTag` (and `pendingSeverity` when no bump is planned); both now print null so every package record has the same keys; schemaVersion unchanged (additive). Other optional fields (`governedBy`, `reason`, `lockfileRefreshResults`, empty `diagnostics`) are still omitted deliberately because absence carries meaning. (4) The `version_command` input of the callisto-action now documents that it is split on whitespace and cannot take quoted arguments or paths with spaces (script unchanged). (5) docs/stability.md Changesets row now says: compatible with `@changesets/cli`; the key is the bare package name unless another ecosystem has a package of that name, then `ecosystem/name` (that is what the code does).\nVerified: new tests run the real binary (duplicate with same and different severity rejected with nothing written; distinct packages still write one changeset), a model test pins the null fields, and an exact help-text test covers version and snapshot; mutations (disable the duplicate check; restore skip_serializing_if) fail them; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Note: E329 follows the E325 to E328 block that PR #500 adds, and both PRs append rows to docs/errors.md, so expect a one-line doc conflict.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 230 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":470,"cache_read_input_tokens":786978,"output_tokens":1202,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":470,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1202,"cache_read_input_tokens":786978,"cache_creation_input_tokens":470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":470},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Gr6G7dz8i92nRpHWdQZCr7":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr503-body","description":"PR body for 503","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr503.diff. Five small consistency fixes from a pre-1.0 audit of docs/stability.md. (1) `callisto add --package cargo/a:patch --package cargo/a:major` wrote both lines into one changeset, which Callisto's own reader then rejected (`status --check` exited 1); `add` now fails with new code E329 (\"package listed more than once in --package\"), writes nothing, and catches bare and qualified spellings of the same package; the interactive wizard cannot produce duplicates. (2) `--strict` help was wrong for `snapshot` (\"Abort if the workspace graph contains error-severity diagnostics\": graph errors abort with or without the flag) and incomplete for `version`; both now say what the flag does. (3) `status --format json` printed `lastReleasedVersion: null` but omitted `lastTag` (and `pendingSeverity` when no bump is planned); both now print null so every package record has the same keys; schemaVersion unchanged (additive). Other optional fields (`governedBy`, `reason`, `lockfileRefreshResults`, empty `diagnostics`) are still omitted deliberately because absence carries meaning. (4) The `version_command` input of the callisto-action now documents that it is split on whitespace and cannot take quoted arguments or paths with spaces (script unchanged). (5) docs/stability.md Changesets row now says: compatible with `@changesets/cli`; the key is the bare package name unless another ecosystem has a package of that name, then `ecosystem/name` (that is what the code does).\nVerified: new tests run the real binary (duplicate with same and different severity rejected with nothing written; distinct packages still write one changeset), a model test pins the null fields, and an exact help-text test covers version and snapshot; mutations (disable the duplicate check; restore skip_serializing_if) fail them; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. Note: E329 follows the E325 to E328 block that PR #500 adds, and both PRs append rows to docs/errors.md, so expect a one-line doc conflict.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 230 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"62496d3a-760e-4937-bf71-0b5f2095ea46","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgupf1jy6rj654NVaxMe5","requestRef":"bd7b0284-116e-4253-a878-2ecaf35cf50d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6ef184c8-5c5a-4dd0-a4a5-748f119a268f","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:45:50.507Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
