{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"c1b78a01-3990-4a0e-91ea-5388a0a62800","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:45:52.014Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"a5d78a38c3b33787e5b5d9b7008e9de2db1c7b9a9ca69bf894342b554f4e1149","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"bd7b0284-116e-4253-a878-2ecaf35cf50d","keep":1267,"tail":["57b85fcf83e0852f44784e2c6f190f34720f9e007258eec70844eac985a51195","b8b5cad74977b6dc7adc5ad07d5eeb3de15722f3769aa5915518d625dfe23097","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1269,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"ed4f26ecf7fd25919ab372989d9b57e3d051ca6e7f24ec8324743fa7f3419734"}
{"parentUuid":"5498a36a-5c99-4ae4-beb7-ba453917fc73","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgupfgfHL7JYTzV6JuSCE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #503, the cleanup batch, is open and linked to trail 198, and its description is being written. All five local checks pass outside the sandbox, and CI has not run.\n\n**What's in #503**\n- **`add` rejects a duplicate package** with the new E329 and writes nothing, instead of writing a changeset Callisto's own reader rejects.\n- **`status --format json`** prints `lastTag` and `pendingSeverity` as `null`, so every package record has the same keys.\n- **`--strict` help** is corrected for `snapshot` and `version`.\n- **`version_command`** is documented as not taking quoted arguments.\n- **`docs/stability.md`** now says changeset keys are the bare name unless ambiguous, which is the bare-names decision you approved.\n\n**Open PRs, in merge order**\n1. **#500** (error codes), which unblocks the follow-ups.\n2. **#501** (input validation, a one-line `docs/errors.md` fix from me) and **#503** (also a one-line `docs/errors.md` conflict, since both append rows).\n3. **#502** (exit code 2): I'll classify E325 to E329 in it once #500 and #503 land.\n4. **#498, #499, #495 and #497** are independent.\n\n**For the 1.0 picture:** these seven PRs close every high-confidence finding from the stability audit except the two follow-ups from #500: E254 as a catch-all, and the E171 sites in `release/binding.rs` and `release/derive.rs` that look reachable through config. I'd take those next, after the merges, with a check for user-reachable cases first.\n\nneeds input: merge #500 first and tell me, and I'll update #501, #502 and #503."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1434,"cache_read_input_tokens":787448,"output_tokens":554,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens"