{"parentUuid":"d92c9b19-38ab-4201-8ea2-87f239621290","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"046082fd-2080-4f3d-baad-99cd66b24a71","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:46:14.092Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"c03d2eb9cd8ec74ac1d50816902b02c873dbfca0d4ed6b981be6f28615a0ee0a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RegxLkKATLTgRafA82jJr1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr503_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\nA pre-1.0 audit of `docs/stability.md` found five places where Callisto's output, help or docs disagreed with what it does.\n\n- `callisto add --package cargo/a:patch --package cargo/a:major` wrote both lines into one changeset, and Callisto's own reader then rejected the file (`status --check` exited 1). `add` now fails with new code E329 and writes nothing. Bare and qualified spellings of the same package are caught. The interactive wizard cannot produce duplicates.\n- `--strict` help was wrong for `snapshot` (graph errors abort with or without the flag) and incomplete for `version`. Both now say what the flag does.\n- `status --format json` printed `lastReleasedVersion: null` but omitted `lastTag` and, with no bump planned, `pendingSeverity`. Both now print `null`, so every package record has the same keys. `schemaVersion` is unchanged because the change is additive. `governedBy`, `reason`, `lockfileRefreshResults` and empty `diagnostics` are still omitted on purpose, since absence carries meaning there.\n- The `version_command` input of `callisto-action` now documents that it is split on whitespace and cannot take quoted arguments or paths with spaces. The script is unchanged.\n- The `docs/stability.md` Changesets row now matches the code: compatible with `@changesets/cli`, with a bare package name as the key unless another ecosystem has a package of that name.\n\nNote: E329 follows E325 to E328, which PR #500 adds. Both PRs append a row to `docs/errors.md`, so expect a one-line conflict there.\n\n## Verify\n\nNew tests run the real binary. A duplicate with the same or a different severity is rejected with nothing written, and distinct packages still write one changeset. A model test pins the null fields, and an exact help-text test covers `version` and `snapshot`. Disabling the duplicate check or restoring `skip_serializing_if` fails these tests. `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BiMgB965WoECEFNVE5Y4Hw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 503 --title \"fix(cli): reject duplicate packages in add and align status JSON and docs\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr503_final.md; gh pr list --state open --json number,headRefName --jq '.[]|\"\\(.number) \\(.headRefName)\"'","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
