{"parentUuid":"046082fd-2080-4f3d-baad-99cd66b24a71","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguphKDFu72Sfazc32XMH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #503 now has its description, and the body keeps the E329 and `docs/errors.md` merge note.\n\nAll nine of my PRs are open and waiting on review. No agents are running.\n\n| PR | What |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| #495 | Changeset process docs |\n| #497 | Matrix ordering test |\n| #498 | camelCase JSON keys |\n| #499 | `release pending` envelope |\n| #500 | One condition per error code |\n| #501 | Reject unknown group keys and invalid `pre enter` tags |\n| #502 | Exit 2 for usage errors |\n| #503 | Cleanup batch, including E329 for duplicate packages |\n\n#493 is the automated release PR for 0.20.0. Its changelog will carry the entries from everything above once these merge.\n\n**Merge order:** #500 first, then #501 and #503, then #502. I handle the one-line `docs/errors.md` fixes and the exit-code classification of E325 to E329, as soon as you say each merged.\n\n**Why I'm stopping here.** Everything I can safely do next stacks on these PRs. The two remaining 1.0 candidates, E254 as a catch-all and the user-reachable E171 sites, touch the same error code area as #500, so starting them now would repeat the overlap mistakes. I'll take them right after #500 merges.\n\nneeds input: please review and merge, starting with #500."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1261,"cache_read_input_tokens":790441,"output_tokens":457,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1261,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":457,"cache_read_input_tokens":790441,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1261,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1261},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9ef2c0a1-4756-4bfb-9ecb-0198ec72a78d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CguphJtQBAtkysTV4Jmgc","requestRef":"884ff21c-066e-4b3a-a174-a6dffb48a340","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bc04259b-e704-4eda-97a5-16d9228168dc","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:46:18.303Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
