{"parentUuid":"c6fc8124-0304-4cd9-9bee-a63d6588b39c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e95bf985-f2d8-4dab-90b1-65f5bd257287","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:03:21.377Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"f5dadeadb6ad17ba28730893b30df25a07030d925ebebab3381e6ae3800e7972","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The envelope tests are about the JSON shape, and exit codes now have their own classification tests. So the helper should expect the exit code that the error's own code implies, not a hard-coded 1."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0185r5ufK6Z2Pg8Fs2wLMwxH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/fix_envelope_helper.py","content":"p = \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004/crates/callisto-cli/tests/error_envelope_tests.rs\"\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"    let out = callisto(dir, args);\n    assert_eq!(out.status.code(), Some(1), \"args {args:?}\");\n    let stderr = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr);\n    serde_json::from_str(&stderr)\n        .unwrap_or_else(|error| panic!(\"stderr of {args:?} is not only JSON ({error}): {stderr}\"))\n}\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    let out = callisto(dir, args);\n    let stderr = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr);\n    let envelope: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(&stderr)\n        .unwrap_or_else(|error| panic!(\"stderr of {args:?} is not only JSON ({error}): {stderr}\"));\n    // A usage error exits 2 and every other failure exits 1; the classification has its own tests.\n    let code = envelope[\"error\"][\"code\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default();\n    let expected = if callisto_cli::error::USAGE_CODES.contains(&code) { 2 } else { 1 };\n    assert_eq!(out.status.code(), Some(expected), \"args {args:?}: {code}\");\n    envelope\n}\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s.replace(old, new))\nprint(\"ok\")\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MktNjqBZRgAjNEzbBp5Spw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/fix_envelope_helper.py && cargo fmt && cargo test -p callisto-cli --test error_envelope_tests 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test |test result|panicked|^error\" | head","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true,"timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
