{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","prNumber":501,"prUrl":"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/501","prRepository":"orin-dx/callisto","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:07:15.244Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d3a846a6-49af-44d2-9dce-ac5fbb855e17","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgurJFX6pyLjKYopwze9k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`fix/cli-polish` (#503) is resolved and pushed. It also repairs main, which is red right now. **Merge #503 first.**\n\n**Why main is red.** #500 and #502 merged, and each was green on its own. Together they break two tests. This is the semantic collision I flagged earlier:\n1. **#502's classification test** requires every documented error code to be classified. #500 added E325 to E328, so they were unclassified.\n2. **#499's envelope test** asserted exit 1 for every failing command. Since #502, `--dry-run` on `release build-python` is a usage error and exits 2.\n\nThe last CI run on main (`b00c8c03a`, the #502 merge) failed.\n\n**What #503 now carries**\n- **Conflict resolved:** the `docs/errors.md` rows for E327 and E329.\n- **Classification:** E327 and E329 are usage errors and exit 2. E325, E326 and E328 are runtime and exit 1. The duplicate-package test now expects 2.\n- **Envelope test fix:** the helper expects the exit code its error code implies, 2 if the code is a usage code, otherwise 1. The classification has its own tests.\n- **Checks:** all five pass outside the sandbox. The commit is signed.\n\n**#501:** I resolved its one `docs/errors.md` conflict, where the E324 wording and the E327 row overlap, and pushed it. It will fail the same inherited test until #503 lands, so after #503 merges I'll merge main into #501 once more.\n\n**Why this slipped past me:** I predicted the classification collision and planned to fix it after the merge, but the second one, the envelope test, I didn't see coming. Neither PR touched the other's files, so no conflict check could catch it. The lesson I'll keep: when two PRs both change observable behavior (exit codes, error codes), run the other's tests against the combination before merging, not just a textual conflict check.\n\nneeds input: merge #503, then tell me, and I'll finish #501."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1251,"cache_read_input_tokens":809564,"output_tokens":650,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1251,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":650,"cache_read_input_tokens":809564,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1251},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d2e70327-988a-4649-9e3e-c446065477dd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgurJF7Hq7kkUds7ZaKxW","requestRef":"d4d5050e-3e1f-4826-a7c1-ce11dee19b4b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"54602cf8-f14a-4d2f-a82c-8f80d7067a9e","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:07:20.487Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a99fea3d03893e29f","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/input-validation","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
