{"parentUuid":"7295328f-2cb0-4097-a4fc-742a35d4e66d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CguskdCRWuQJZFZDNwN4A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The #501 CI failures aren't from its change. They come from main, which is red on two tests, and #503 fixes both and is fully green: all 17 of its checks pass.\n\n**The failures on #501**\n- **Envelope test:** `failing_release_commands_keep_schema_version_and_report_dry_run` expects exit 1, but `--dry-run` on `release build-python` now exits 2 (#502).\n- **Classification test:** after fixing the first, I found a second one that fail-fast had been hiding. `every_documented_code_is_classified_usage_or_runtime_exactly_once` fails because E325 to E328 from #500 are unclassified.\n- Both fail on main for the same reason, and the failing test logs match.\n\n**Why I didn't patch #501 directly.** The fix touches the same lines as #503, where E329 gets classified too. Duplicating it here would create a new conflict, and I'd rather not stack another. I reverted my trial edit, so #501's branch is unchanged: its own checks pass locally, and Code Coverage plus both Test Suite jobs fail only on those two inherited tests.\n\n**Next step:** merge #503, which turns main green. Then tell me, and I'll merge main into #501 once more and push, which gets it to a clean run. Nothing in #501 itself needs to change.\n\nneeds input: merge #503, then tell me, and I'll refresh #501."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":275,"cache_read_input_tokens":816772,"output_tokens":453,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":275,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":453,"cache_rea