{"parentUuid":"a9c313ad-9260-44dc-bfb5-3f818a2b4170","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvHTZWjtNpX6exjuA53V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The error-envelope work is **#499, and it's merged** (main commit `c06472863`, branch `fix/error-envelope`).\n\n**What it did**\n- **Finding:** the trail's main complaint was already fixed on main. A failing `release plan` already reported `command: \"release plan\"`, and the `release-pr` subcommands already reported their own names. The implementer proved that by running the built binary for every command.\n- **Added:**\n  - `release pending` and the hidden `release build-python` now emit the standard envelope (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`), with their payloads unchanged.\n  - A failing run names its own subcommand instead of `release`.\n  - New tests assert the error envelope for every command family, with and without `--dry-run`.\n  - Spec REL-CMD-12 lists both commands.\n- **Left alone:** `release inspect` success prints the raw input document, with no envelope.\n\n**Follow-ups it needed**\n- Its envelope test later had to learn about exit code 2 (#502), which I fixed in #503 and #501 as part of getting main green.\n- The exit-code work in #502 and the camelCase work in #498 came from the same trail, #177.\n\n**Trails.** I checked the done-when text and closed #177 (the failing commands print the same envelope keys as their success reports, with a test) and #178 (the one missing test merged in #497). #198 stays open, since #503 is still pending under it.\n\nneeds input: none."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829655,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":957,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":483},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_i