eptable under the promise and report it, do not change it without evidence it is wrong.\n\nRequired:\n1. Enumerate EVERY command and subcommand that accepts `--format json` (read crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs and the command handlers; include hidden CI-plumbing ones). For each, find what its SUCCESS output looks like, with the built binary where the command can run offline in a small temp workspace (a git repo with a Cargo workspace and `callisto init --yes`). Build a table: command, success output has schemaVersion (yes/no), command key, dryRun key, camelCase keys (yes/no), notes. Include `schema`, `completions` (not JSON, say so), `matrix`, `compose-pr-body`, `release plan|execute|inspect|artifact-manifest|build-python|pending`, `release-pr verify|decide|commit-plan`, `status`, `version`, `snapshot`, `pre`, `add`, `init`.\n2. Fix any gap in a Rust report type with the standard envelope (follow how ReleasePendingReport was added in crates/callisto-model/src/release/report.rs), keeping the payload keys unchanged.\n3. Add ONE table-driven test that runs the real binary for every command that can run offline with `--format json` and asserts: valid JSON on stdout, top-level `schemaVersion` is a number, and (for reports that have them) `command` equals the documented command name and `dryRun` is a bool; and fails with a message naming any command missing it. Commands that cannot run offline in a test (needs network or toolchain) are listed in the test as an explicit allow-list with a reason, so a new command forces a decision.\n4. Also check the callisto-action outputs (.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml and the scripts that set them) against docs/stability.md: the Stable table says the action INPUTS are stable; list the inputs and outputs in docs as they exist and note any that are undocumented or inconsistently named (do not rename anything; report).\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies. Do NOT add a changeset; return in plain words what a script sees now versus before for any output you changed. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-model`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check on the table test (remove a report's schemaVersion and confirm it fails). If you add error codes, they must be classified in crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs / tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs (see that test). Final report: the command table, fixes, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5cd8af54-84ad-48e2-ae3e-10ac41280718","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgwShjxUJ3RtKozBcncxt","requestRef":"58e959c1-2b69-467c-af35-fdf6f4fe77c2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b67e19f0-5cd4-452c-9bc8-bce3d3e115cb","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:19:36.135Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"b67e19f0-5cd4-452c-9bc8-bce3d3e115cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwShke9y7Be1h6LmaqcE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014x9UxcCV9E5ed8Qhx2TKBk","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"perf-scale","description":"Find and fix scaling hotspots","prompt":"Task: find and fix the next performance hotspot in Callisto when a monorepo is very large. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first (it forbids a git process per package) and follow it.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c perf/scale-hotspots origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nAlready measured and fixed: on a synthetic workspace of 1,800 packages (1,500 Cargo crates in a dependency chain plus 300 npm packages) `status`, `version --dry-run` and `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` are flat in package count (8 to 23 git processes, under about 2.6 s on a debug build), and the unreleased-changes check was changed from one `git diff` per changed package to one per tag commit. A benchmark harness is at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/perf_bench.sh (read it; it builds a temp repo, shims `git` to count processes, and times four commands; env N = cargo crates, M = npm packages, CH = changed packages, BIN = the callisto binary). Copy it to your own scratch location rather than editing it.\n\nUnmeasured dimensions to test, each with a real run and numbers (processes, wall time, scaling from small to large):\n1. Many pending changesets: 200, 1,000 and 3,000 changeset files each naming one or a few packages, then `status`, `version --dry-run`, `version --emit-preview`, `compose-pr-body`. Look for super-linear time (quadratic merging or sorting) and for one file read or one git call per changeset.\n2. Many tags: 5,000 and 20,000 tags (several tags per package, as a long-lived repo has), then the same commands. Look for work per tag beyond one `git tag` / `for-each-ref` call.\n3. A long history: 20,000 commits on main; commands that walk history (`status`, `version` with commit inference if enabled, unreleased-changes, `release plan`).\n4. A wide dependency graph: 1,500 packages where many depend on one core package (fan-out), and a deep chain; cascade planning.\n5. Startup cost on a tiny repo (cold `callisto --help` and `status`), release build numbers for the main commands at 1,800 packages (build release with `cargo build --release -p callisto-cli`; it takes a few minutes).\n\nMethod: measure first, then fix only hotspots where the improvement is at least 2x at the large scale or removes a per-item process or a quadratic loop. For each fix, keep results identical (differential or golden tests), add a test that pins the call count or complexity (use the existing RecordingGit-style runners in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs tests as a pattern), and re-run the same measurement to show before and after. If everything is already flat, say so with the numbers, and do not invent a change.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change per hotspot; no new dependencies; match surrounding comment density. Do NOT add a changeset; return in plain words what a user with a large repo gets. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check on each new test. Final report: the measurement table (dimension, small, large, scaling verdict), each fix with before and after numbers, files changed, new tests, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840026,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7660,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1372},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840026,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7660,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840026},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014x9UxcCV9E5ed8Qhx2TKBk":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"perf-scale","description":"Find and fix scaling hotspots","prompt":"Task: find and fix the next performance hotspot in Callisto when a monorepo is very large. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first (it forbids a git process per package) and follow it.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c perf/scale-hotspots origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nAlready measured and fixed: on a synthetic workspace of 1,800 packages (1,500 Cargo crates in a dependency chain plus 300 npm packages) `status`, `version --dry-run` and `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` are flat in package count (8 to 23 git processes, under about 2.6 s on a debug build), and the unreleased-changes check was changed from one `git diff` per changed package to one per tag commit. A benchmark harness is at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/perf_bench.sh (read it; it builds a temp repo, shims `git` to count processes, and times four commands; env N = cargo crates, M = npm packages, CH = changed packages, BIN = the callisto binary). Copy it to your own scratch location rather than editing it.\n\nUnmeasured dimensions to test, each with a real run and numbers (processes, wall time, scaling from small to large):\n1. Many pending changesets: 200, 1,000 and 3,000 changeset files each naming one or a few packages, then `status`, `version --dry-run`, `version --emit-preview`, `compose-pr-body`. Look for super-linear time (quadratic merging or sorting) and for one file read or one git call per changeset.\n2. Many tags: 5,000 and 20,000 tags (several tags per package, as a long-lived repo has), then the same commands. Look for work per tag beyond one `git tag` / `for-each-ref` call.\n3. A long history: 20,000 commits on main; commands that walk history (`status`, `version` with commit inference if enabled, unreleased-changes, `release plan`).\n4. A wide dependency graph: 1,500 packages where many depend on one core package (fan-out), and a deep chain; cascade planning.\n5. Startup cost on a tiny repo (cold `callisto --help` and `status`), release build numbers for the main commands at 1,800 packages (build release with `cargo build --release -p callisto-cli`; it takes a few minutes).\n\nMethod: measure first, then fix only hotspots where the improvement is at least 2x at the large scale or removes a per-item process or a quadratic loop. For each fix, keep results identical (differential or golden tests), add a test that pins the call count or complexity (use the existing RecordingGit-style runners in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs tests as a pattern), and re-run the same measurement to show before and after. If everything is already flat, say so with the numbers, and do not invent a change.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change per hotspot; no new dependencies; match surrounding comment density. Do NOT add a changeset; return in plain words what a user with a large repo gets. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check on each new test. Final report: the measurement table (dimension, small, large, scaling verdict), each fix with before and after numbers, files changed, new tests, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5cd8af54-84ad-48e2-ae3e-10ac41280718","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CgwShjxUJ3RtKozBcncxt","requestRef":"58e959c1-2b69-467c-af35-fdf6f4fe77c2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"07f54a94-03c4-4323-9e58-605c8a15fbfd","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:19:46.022Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"07f54a94-03c4-4323-9e58-605c8a15fbfd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwShke9y7Be1h6LmaqcE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PZxScRkuubxAgc2wKsiEK5","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"smith:implementer","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","name":"stability-contract-tests","description":"Pin tag names and Action inputs","prompt":"Task: add contract tests for the remaining 1.0 stable promises that have no test, test-only. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c test/stability-contracts origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\ndocs/stability.md says these are stable from 1.0. For each, first check whether a test already pins it (grep the tests and the .github/tests scripts), then add one where it is missing; report what already existed:\n1. Tag names: the default tag is `{name}@{version}`, and `ecosystem/name@{version}` once another ecosystem has a package of that name; `tag-template` pins a name. Test with the real binary and temp workspaces (see crates/callisto-cli/tests for patterns): single ecosystem uses the bare name; two ecosystems with the same package name both switch to the qualified form (and the output of `status` or the release plan shows it); a `tag-template` overrides both.\n2. The GitHub Actions: the inputs of `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto` are stable. Write a contract test (Rust or the repo's existing shell contract-test style under .github/tests and .github/actions/*/tests; prefer extending the existing pattern and run `just workflow-contracts`) that pins the set of input names and their `required`/default values from each action.yml against a checked-in list, so removing or renaming an input fails CI and adding one requires updating the list deliberately. Do NOT change the action files. The repo's workflow policy check (.github/tests/verify-release-workflow-policy.sh) forbids new secrets and write permissions; your change must not need any.\n3. Exit codes 0/1/2: the classification test exists (crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs); only add a test if you find a promise gap, and report it.\n4. `callisto.toml`: a test already rejects an unknown key in every table (crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs `every_config_table_rejects_an_unknown_key`); verify it still covers every table struct currently in config/ (a table added later must be caught: consider a test that fails when a config struct has no deny_unknown_fields) and add that guard if cheap.\n\nMutation check each new test. No code or action changes unless a test reveals a real bug (then stop and report it with evidence). Do NOT add a changeset (tests only). Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just workflow-contracts` judged by exit code (the sandbox blocks three network tests and gpg-signing in workflow-contracts; if so say so). Final report: per promise, what existed, what you added (test name and file), the mutation used, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840026,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7660,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1372},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840026,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7660,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840026},"type":"message"}]