{"parentUuid":"b67e19f0-5cd4-452c-9bc8-bce3d3e115cb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fddf1b3c-8d23-4438-96c6-01148de494a2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XcZWC1AaKHkMzbZMDzXTXR","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: aafeb13134f6a0ae4 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'aafeb13134f6a0ae4', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/aafeb13134f6a0ae4.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"63f87ddb-8ca4-48ec-97cd-d820a8853545","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:20:00.896Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"aafeb13134f6a0ae4","description":"Pin schemaVersion on every JSON output","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Task: make sure EVERY `--format json` output carries `schemaVersion`, and pin it with a test, because docs/stability.md freezes this from 1.0 (\"Every report carries schemaVersion\"). Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first and follow them.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c fix/json-contract-complete origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nKnown: the previous PRs added envelope-checking tests for FAILING commands (crates/callisto-cli/tests/error_envelope_tests.rs) and a camelCase guard (crates/callisto-cli/tests/schema_guard_test.rs), and put `release pending` and `release build-python` into the standard envelope. `release inspect` success deliberately prints the raw input document (a durable document with its own versioning); decide from the code whether that is acceptable under the promise and report it, do not change it without evidence it is wrong.\n\nRequired:\n1. Enumerate EVERY command and subcommand that accepts `--format json` (read crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs and the command handlers; include hidden CI-plumbing ones). For each, find what its SUCCESS output looks like, with the built binary where the command can run offline in a small temp workspace (a git repo with a Cargo workspace and `callisto init --yes`). Build a table: command, success output has schemaVersion (yes/no), command key, dryRun key, camelCase keys (yes/no), notes. Include `schema`, `completions` (not JSON, say so), `matrix`, `compose-pr-body`, `release plan|execute|inspect|artifact-manifest|build-python|pending`, `release-pr verify|decide|commit-plan`, `status`, `version`, `snapshot`, `pre`, `add`, `init`.\n2. Fix any gap in a Rust report type with the standard envelope (follow how ReleasePendingReport was added in crates/callisto-model/src/release/report.rs), keeping the payload keys unchanged.\n3. Add ONE table-driven test that runs the real binary for every command that can run offline with `--format json` and asserts: valid JSON on stdout, top-level `schemaVersion` is a number, and (for reports that have them) `command` equals the documented command name and `dryRun` is a bool; and fails with a message naming any command missing it. Commands that cannot run offline in a test (needs network or toolchain) are listed in the test as an explicit allow-list with a reason, so a new command forces a decision.\n4. Also check the callisto-action outputs (.github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml and the scripts that set them) against docs/stability.md: the Stable table says the action INPUTS are stable; list the inputs and outputs in docs as they exist and note any that are undocumented or inconsistently named (do not rename anything; report).\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change; no new dependencies. Do NOT add a changeset; return in plain words what a script sees now versus before for any output you changed. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli -p callisto-model`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check on the table test (remove a report's schemaVersion and confirm it fails). If you add error codes, they must be classified in crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs / tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs (see that test). Final report: the command table, fixes, new test names, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/aafeb13134f6a0ae4.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5cd8af54-84ad-48e2-ae3e-10ac41280718","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","branch":"fix/cli-polish","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b67e19f0-5cd4-452c-9bc8-bce3d3e115cb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"63f87ddb-8ca4-48ec-97cd-d820a8853545","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Agent","toolUseID":"toolu_01XcZWC1AaKHkMzbZMDzXTXR","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"agent-a528198a629670004\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Agent\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":73},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3125da1c-84e5-4584-8bcd-5061e014ad05","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:20:00.896Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"07f54a94-03c4-4323-9e58-605c8a15fbfd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fddf1b3c-8d23-4438-96c6-01148de494a2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014x9UxcCV9E5ed8Qhx2TKBk","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a3658a1f85bca2d75 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a3658a1f85bca2d75', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a3658a1f85bca2d75.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"257adc77-59b1-4dff-b4a6-a24b7f8d8a7f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:20:00.943Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a3658a1f85bca2d75","description":"Find and fix scaling hotspots","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Task: find and fix the next performance hotspot in Callisto when a monorepo is very large. Repo: Callisto (Rust release tool). Read AGENTS.md first (it forbids a git process per package) and follow it.\n\nSetup: first `git switch -c perf/scale-hotspots origin/main` (the local origin/main ref is current; you cannot fetch). If the branch exists, switch to it. Work only here.\n\nAlready measured and fixed: on a synthetic workspace of 1,800 packages (1,500 Cargo crates in a dependency chain plus 300 npm packages) `status`, `version --dry-run` and `compose-pr-body --publish-plan` are flat in package count (8 to 23 git processes, under about 2.6 s on a debug build), and the unreleased-changes check was changed from one `git diff` per changed package to one per tag commit. A benchmark harness is at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/perf_bench.sh (read it; it builds a temp repo, shims `git` to count processes, and times four commands; env N = cargo crates, M = npm packages, CH = changed packages, BIN = the callisto binary). Copy it to your own scratch location rather than editing it.\n\nUnmeasured dimensions to test, each with a real run and numbers (processes, wall time, scaling from small to large):\n1. Many pending changesets: 200, 1,000 and 3,000 changeset files each naming one or a few packages, then `status`, `version --dry-run`, `version --emit-preview`, `compose-pr-body`. Look for super-linear time (quadratic merging or sorting) and for one file read or one git call per changeset.\n2. Many tags: 5,000 and 20,000 tags (several tags per package, as a long-lived repo has), then the same commands. Look for work per tag beyond one `git tag` / `for-each-ref` call.\n3. A long history: 20,000 commits on main; commands that walk history (`status`, `version` with commit inference if enabled, unreleased-changes, `release plan`).\n4. A wide dependency graph: 1,500 packages where many depend on one core package (fan-out), and a deep chain; cascade planning.\n5. Startup cost on a tiny repo (cold `callisto --help` and `status`), release build numbers for the main commands at 1,800 packages (build release with `cargo build --release -p callisto-cli`; it takes a few minutes).\n\nMethod: measure first, then fix only hotspots where the improvement is at least 2x at the large scale or removes a per-item process or a quadratic loop. For each fix, keep results identical (differential or golden tests), add a test that pins the call count or complexity (use the existing RecordingGit-style runners in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs tests as a pattern), and re-run the same measurement to show before and after. If everything is already flat, say so with the numbers, and do not invent a change.\n\nConstraints: smallest complete change per hotspot; no new dependencies; match surrounding comment density. Do NOT add a changeset; return in plain words what a user with a large repo gets. Do not commit, push or sign. Verify with `cargo test -p callisto-graph -p callisto-cli`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` judged by exit code, plus a mutation check on each new test. Final report: the measurement table (dimension, small, large, scaling verdict), each fix with before and after numbers, files changed, new tests, commands with exit codes, and anything you are unsure of.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a3658a1f85bca2d75.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5cd8af54-84ad-48e2-ae3e-10ac41280718","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","branch":"fix/cli-polish","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"07f54a94-03c4-4323-9e58-605c8a15fbfd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
