{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytxL4nYq1T7cJBdRjiu","lastSequenceNum":8710,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"7e3f61e8-a0da-4c1b-8468-011a745737d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwSnAYCozQu1QT3GRV8y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Five agents are running against current main, and #493 (the 0.20.0 release PR) should stay unmerged until they land.\n\n| Agent | Type and model | Goal |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `error-code-reach` | implementer, Sonnet | Splits E254's several conditions into their own codes, and decides for each of the ~45 E171 sites whether a user can actually reach it. It must classify each new code for exit 1 or 2, which is the lesson from the red main. |\n| `json-contract-complete` | implementer, Sonnet | Enumerates every command's `--format json` output and fixes any missing `schemaVersion`. A table-driven test makes a new command force a decision. It also lists the Action's inputs and outputs. |\n| `perf-scale` | implementer, Sonnet | Measures what I haven't yet: thousands of changesets, tens of thousands of tags, a 20,000-commit history, a wide dependency graph, and release-build numbers at 1,800 packages. It fixes only hotspots with at least a 2x gain, and says so if everything is already flat. |\n| `stability-contract-tests` | implementer, Sonnet | Test-only. Pins tag-name rules, the Action input set, and a guard that fails when a config table lacks `deny_unknown_fields`. |\n| `release-safety-audit` | bug-hunter, Sonnet, read-only | Checks trail #162: whether retry and the stale-release-PR guard exist today, and whether a stale release PR can still merge without a failing check. |\n\n**Design choices**\n- **Release safety is investigate-first.** Your rule is that features go in Rust, not shell, so the audit proposes a minimal design instead of editing the release script.\n- **Overlap.** `error-code-reach` and `json-contract-complete` could both touch the error and report files, so I'll run the pairwise check, and also run each branch's tests against the others' combinations before pushing.\n\nI'll review each result, run the full checks outside the sandbox, write the changesets in the layered shape, and tell you when 0.20.0 is ready to read.\n\nneeds input: none. I'll report as each agent finishes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12762,"cache_read_input_tokens":840026,"output_tokens":709,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12762,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":709,"cache_read_input_tokens":840026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12762},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6d8469db-ecbf-4bc9-9f06-b7b5be54eefd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwSn9yxDYKhe1fzrKro6","requestRef":"b4f9e469-0cc2-4a35-a794-d377b3d5b2aa","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6cd20260-77c9-4573-9af7-f6eeee049eee","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:20:07.065Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
