{"parentUuid":"7dd6a7c0-5b81-4490-b6da-97b4c16f4941","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dbe54410-72a6-4175-af43-743ec0bb0be4","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:21:21.674Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"6ddf0bdaf2f04ffa1b5075451904c8d4da40153f00a5bd53a5b8b6df9a100fe6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The audit answers the open question on trail #162 with evidence. Most of its plan is already built, and the one remaining gap is smaller than the trail implied. I'm recording the findings in the trail description, then I'll tell you what I recommend."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017ezsiiNNR48mJmkABNiaA8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/trail162_note.py","content":"import subprocess\n\nnote = (\n    \"Audit (2026-11-11, origin/main f06bb0fd5), plan item by item. \"\n    \"1 Revert the bad merge: done. \"\n    \"2 Retry with backoff and visible stderr: done (gh_retry in create-or-update-release-pr.sh, 4 attempts, REL-PR-08, tested). \"\n    \"3 Pre-merge guard: built as a hold, not a check (REL-PR-09, hold-release-pr.yml drafts the release PR on every push to main; the action marks it ready only if main's tip still equals the commit it built from). A failed or missing refresh leaves a draft, and a draft cannot be merged. \"\n    \"4 Docs: E165 recovery is in docs/releasing.md; `callisto release pending` does not name it. \"\n    \"5 Stray-tag status warning: nothing recorded. \"\n    \"Remaining ways a stale release PR can still merge: a one-call race between the tip read and `gh pr ready`; a delayed or failed hold run; and a person marking the held draft ready by hand, which nothing stops. In each case nothing is published and the first visible failure is the post-merge Release run with E165, repeated on every push until the release payload is reverted.\"\n)\nshown = subprocess.run([\"entire\", \"trail\", \"show\", \"162\", \"--project\", \"gh/orin-dx\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\nbody = shown.split(\"Description:\\n\", 1)[1].strip() if \"Description:\\n\" in shown else \"\"\nr = subprocess.run([\"entire\", \"trail\", \"update\", \"162\", \"--project\", \"gh/orin-dx\", \"--body\", body + \"\\n\\n\" + note], capture_output=True, text=True)\nprint(\"exit\", r.returncode)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016iYT6fFBXKMeDFJgjgxKtj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/trail162_note.py","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
