{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"cbf7089b-2fe5-4925-ba3d-23db0a7796a3","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:21:21.720Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"a5d78a38c3b33787e5b5d9b7008e9de2db1c7b9a9ca69bf894342b554f4e1149","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"3430a937-b4db-4d63-bfbf-42cbd2e97ddd","keep":1450,"tail":["6ddf0bdaf2f04ffa1b5075451904c8d4da40153f00a5bd53a5b8b6df9a100fe6","ca997e62a63a7f13c83a3255af258a4bba1baa47ca751c578c86f5f7c06d84b5","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1452,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"17c9222f21be0c3e1329cce51bf64da7d2c48a330fd18722a4dc9d8179ae512a"}
{"parentUuid":"dbe54410-72a6-4175-af43-743ec0bb0be4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwSt712uq8yqqo6wu8US","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The release-safety audit is back, and trail #162 is in much better shape than its description suggested. The findings are recorded in the trail description.\n\n**Plan items 1, 2 and 3 are done or substantially done**\n- **Reverting the bad merge:** done, and documented as the recovery.\n- **Retries:** `gh_retry` in the release script makes 4 attempts with backoff and prints each failed attempt's stderr, tested under REL-PR-08.\n- **The guard:** built as a hold, not a check. The Hold workflow drafts the open release PR on every push to main, and the release action only marks it ready if main's tip still equals the commit it built from. A failed or missing refresh leaves a draft, and a draft can't be merged. It's tested under REL-PR-09.\n\n**What's still open**\n- **The real gap:** a person can click \"Ready for review\" on a held draft and merge it. Nothing stops that. Two narrower holes remain: a one-call race, and a delayed hold run. In every case **nothing is published**. The first sign is the Release run failing with E165 after the merge, repeating on each push until the release payload is reverted.\n- **Item 4:** the recovery is in `docs/releasing.md`, but `callisto release pending` doesn't point to it.\n- **Item 5, the stray-tag status warning:** nothing recorded.\n\n**My recommendation: don't build a new `release-pr check` command.**\n- A check on the PR would not stop a manual merge, because required status checks aren't enabled on main, which you decided against earlier.\n- It also can't run on the bot-created release PR, for the same reason #484 failed: PRs opened with `GITHUB_TOKEN` start no workflows.\n- The existing design already guarantees nothing is published. A new command would only change when the failure is announced, so it doesn't earn its complexity.\n\n**What I'd do instead, cheap and in Rust or docs only**\n1. Have the E165 error's help text point at the recovery section, so the failure message says what to do.\n2. Optionally, have `callisto release pending` name it too.\n\nI'd add those to the next batch, and close #162 with this decision recorded.\n\nneeds input: a yes on the two small E165 help changes, and tell me if you want a stricter guard despite the cost."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2340,"cache_read_input_tokens":858073,"output_tokens":737,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2340,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":737,"cache_read_input_tokens":858073,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2340},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"32f2ea87-41a6-4d20-a36c-a69f97012771","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwSt6eCsoLsDFZg4kfFa","requestRef":"cbf7089b-2fe5-4925-ba3d-23db0a7796a3","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c555d1e8-ed9c-40f4-9b28-3bf951117078","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:21:28.112Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a528198a629670004","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/cli-polish","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
