{"parentUuid":"927aec5b-5dc0-49fa-b3b3-08ed28d2f1a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwUHN9ccrw13ecUpx4G2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01589sgHzr16D4NhoKX3PBhv","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr505-body","description":"PR body for 505","prompt":"Write the title and body for a test-only pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr505.diff. Change: docs/stability.md freezes `--format json` reports from 1.0 (\"every report carries schemaVersion\"). An audit of every command's JSON success output found every one already carries `schemaVersion`, so no report type changed. A new table-driven test `every_json_success_output_carries_a_schema_version` runs the real binary for 21 invocations across two workspaces (a fresh init+add workspace and a release-commit fixture driven through plan, inspect, artifact-manifest and execute with fake publishers) and asserts stdout is valid JSON with a numeric top-level `schemaVersion`, and for reports that command equals the documented name and `dryRun` is a bool. It walks the clap command tree including hidden commands, so every command must be in the table or an explicit exempt list with a reason (`completions`, `help`, `schema`, `release build-python`), which makes a new command force a decision. The test makes no network calls: the fixture's GitHub-looking `origin` is given an unreachable local proxy in repo config. docs/stability.md gains a sentence: `release inspect` prints the raw intent, manifest or receipt, each with its own `schemaVersion`, and `schema` prints JSON Schema documents, not reports. Findings reported, not changed: the Action's inputs are snake_case and outputs camelCase (`hasChangesets`, `published`, `publishedPackages`), and `schema` output has no schemaVersion.\nVerified: a mutation making `matrix` print JSON without the envelope fails the test; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. No changeset (tests and one doc sentence).\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 200 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":983,"cache_read_input_tokens":900629,"output_tokens":3310,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":983,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3310,"cache_read_input_tokens":900629,"cache_creation_input_tokens":983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":983},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01589sgHzr16D4NhoKX3PBhv":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr505-body","description":"PR body for 505","prompt":"Write the title and body for a test-only pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr505.diff. Change: docs/stability.md freezes `--format json` reports from 1.0 (\"every report carries schemaVersion\"). An audit of every command's JSON success output found every one already carries `schemaVersion`, so no report type changed. A new table-driven test `every_json_success_output_carries_a_schema_version` runs the real binary for 21 invocations across two workspaces (a fresh init+add workspace and a release-commit fixture driven through plan, inspect, artifact-manifest and execute with fake publishers) and asserts stdout is valid JSON with a numeric top-level `schemaVersion`, and for reports that command equals the documented name and `dryRun` is a bool. It walks the clap command tree including hidden commands, so every command must be in the table or an explicit exempt list with a reason (`completions`, `help`, `schema`, `release build-python`), which makes a new command force a decision. The test makes no network calls: the fixture's GitHub-looking `origin` is given an unreachable local proxy in repo config. docs/stability.md gains a sentence: `release inspect` prints the raw intent, manifest or receipt, each with its own `schemaVersion`, and `schema` prints JSON Schema documents, not reports. Findings reported, not changed: the Action's inputs are snake_case and outputs camelCase (`hasChangesets`, `published`, `publishedPackages`), and `schema` output has no schemaVersion.\nVerified: a mutation making `matrix` print JSON without the envelope fails the test; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI. No changeset (tests and one doc sentence).\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 200 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"535e2af2-9136-4a4e-ad06-d1819abee5a8","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CgwUHMkp8MixXSWXzhbj1","requestRef":"f035e4ef-c460-4e3d-86d9-a7c888f4b0c7","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f17cf25-1d6f-40db-903b-3cac5a604c7b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:39:58.513Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5e465e9b44611fbd","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"2f17cf25-1d6f-40db-903b-3cac5a604c7b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwUHN9ccrw13ecUpx4G2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WCMEtYdMrkpHY2Bd7PspiD","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr506-body","description":"PR body for 506","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr506.diff. Change: finishes the error-code cleanup before 1.0 freezes codes (docs/stability.md: a code keeps its meaning and is never reused). E254 (\"unknown callisto key\") had become a catch-all for nine different callisto.toml conditions; an unknown key is already E325, so E254 is retired (listed as never reused). New codes: E330 bad `publish-to`; E331 bad `release-trigger`; E332 bad `cascade.mode`; E333 bad `changelog.layout`; E334 unknown registry `kind`; E335 `publish-url` on a non-PyPI registry; E336 `url` on a Cargo registry; E337 registry timeout outside 1s to 1h; E338 unparsable package `match` pattern. E339: a `[registries.X] kind` that does not match the package's ecosystem; it used to report E171 (\"internal release invariant violated, report it\") although a user can cause it, and is raised at release derivation, not config load. Every new variant carries the file path (the old release-trigger error printed an empty path). All ten are runtime errors (exit 1) and are classified in the exit-code classification test. Of about 40 other `ReleaseInvariant` (E171) sites, only that one was reachable by user input; the rest stay E171 and the agent's table of site-by-site reasons was reviewed (some judged by reading, not reproduced). docs/errors.md, docs/config.md and docs/specs/release.json updated; the changeset is minor with a Breaking note.\nCompatibility: a script matching E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry k