{"parentUuid":"9f05b917-7ea8-4e24-8158-25282fbef3b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwUK6zMKT3pQQxVAyi6V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three of the four agents' work is now in PRs, and the descriptions are being written.\n\n| PR | What | Evidence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **#506** | Retires E254, which had become a catch-all for nine config conditions. Each gets its own code (E330 to E338), and a registry kind that doesn't match the package ecosystem is E339 instead of E171. | Ten tests drive the real binary, with a mutation check. Of ~40 other E171 sites, only that one was user-reachable. |\n| **#505** | A table-driven test that every command's JSON success output carries `schemaVersion`. | The audit found they all already do, so no report type changed. It walks the clap command tree, so a new command forces a decision. The test makes no network calls. |\n| **#504** | Contract tests for the tag names a release actually creates, the input set of both Actions, clap parse exit codes, and a guard that every config struct denies unknown fields. | A mutation per area fails its test. |\n\n**Fixes I made to the agents' work**\n- **#505:** the test would have contacted `github.com` and `crates.io` in CI, because its fixture uses a GitHub-looking `origin`. I made it fully offline by giving the test repo an unreachable local proxy.\n- **#504:** I ran `workflow-contracts` outside the sandbox, which the agent couldn't do, and it passes. The Action input pinning needs no secrets or permissions.\n\n**Checked:** none of the three conflict with each other. All five local checks pass outside the sandbox on each. CI hasn't run. #506's changeset is minor with a `Breaking:` note, and #504 and #505 need no changeset (tests and one doc sentence).\n\n**Still running:** `perf-scale`, the scaling benchmark and fix agent. **Release safety:** I recorded the audit on trail #162 and recommended two small E165 help changes. Say yes and I'll add them.\n\nneeds input: a yes on the E165 help changes, then review #504 to #506. #493 stays unmerged until `perf-scale` reports."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3860,"cache_read_input_tokens":901612,"output_tokens":678,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3860,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":901612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3860},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"429239db-5441-4f53-b95d-e2ae8ba52480","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwUK6dHKRvykzVUPHQpQ","requestRef":"055a81b5-8687-433f-bce2-1737c50b112c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6117cb50-3422-4336-8d5e-165872bd887c","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:40:12.928Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5e465e9b44611fbd","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
