jects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"ae0be0e3-abc5-497e-98e6-c00af99234e0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwVku7adLB8gmEKQHUBe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Az16a6WH52AzAeHMEHbxiG","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","name":"pr507-body","description":"PR body for 507","prompt":"Write the title and body for a pull request in the Callisto repo (a release tool heading to 1.0). Read the diff at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr507.diff. Change: two scaling hotspots found by benchmarking a synthetic monorepo (1,800 packages, 1,500 of them depending on one core package, plus 1,000 pending changesets, 20,000 commits, 20,000 tags), both in the `release` path; status, version --dry-run, version --emit-preview and the other dimensions were already flat or linear. (1) The release preflight (the check that a package has not moved past its version commit) ran one `git log -- <manifest>` and one `git cat-file --batch` per releasing package; it now uses one `git log` for all manifests (new `first_parent_commits_by_path` in callisto-model's vcs access, using `--first-parent -m` and literal pathspecs) plus one batched read, and a package whose newest candidate is not the version-setting commit falls back to its own read, so results are unchanged. (2) `workspace_package` rescanned every package and recomputed identities once per entry, called from selection expansion, the roster, first-release checks, the publish outlook and release gaps; replaced by a map built once (`ReleaseOwners`) with every call site migrated, and per-selection linear `any` scans became set lookups. Measured: fan-out 1,800 packages `release --dry-run` 13.9 s and 3,012 git processes to 1.85 s and 14 (debug), 8.10 s to 1.27 s (release build); with 20,000 commits 7.95 s to 1.63 s; `compose-pr-body` 12.1 s to 1.45 s (debug) and 1.90 s to 0.76 s (release). Old and new output were byte-identical for `release --dry-run` text and JSON and for `compose-pr-body` on both large cases.\nVerified: a counting-runner test pins one `git log` and a bounded `cat-file` count at 3 and at 12 packages (two mutations fail it); a 3,000-package test fails when the index is rebuilt per lookup (18 s vs 0.04 s; it is wall-clock based with about a 250x margin, so a very loaded CI machine is the only flake risk); the existing version-commit tests including a 105-edit and merge-commit cases pass; `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. Not run: CI.\nNot changed, reported: `version --emit-preview` takes 33 to 45 s when thousands of packages are bumped because each manifest and changelog write does a file fsync and a directory fsync (about 75% of the time is macOS F_FULLFSYNC); left alone because it is the durability invariant in AGENTS.md.\nStyle rules (strict): one line per paragraph, never hard-wrap; succinct and plain; no backstory, no filler, no emoji, no session links; sections \"## Summary\" and \"## Verify\"; under 260 words. Return only the title (conventional-commit style, lower case after the type) on the first line, a blank line, then the body."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":971,"cache_read_input_tokens":925431,"output_tokens":1355,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":971,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1355,"cache_read_input_tokens":925431,"cache_creation_input_tokens":971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":971},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"contex