{"parentUuid":"e373b6c1-b835-4160-83e6-d91703297f15","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"29b74c96-835d-4b9a-a902-43c0ad25f09a","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:59:41.929Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"308d07fe8001e7115474cab4bef9971b9ee30386529fe5c5a2a24e2902d05a63","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The narrator's text is accurate, but it splits nearly every sentence into its own paragraph. I'm regrouping it into proper paragraphs, with the same facts."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DCdA2xe6Qj64GNMuEmRrPx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr507_final.md","content":"## Summary\n\nPlanning a release in a very large monorepo scaled with the number of releasing packages, so `callisto release` and the release PR body slowed sharply as more packages shipped together. Two causes, found by the same benchmark on one planning path:\n\n- The preflight that checks a package has not moved past its version commit ran one `git log` and one `git cat-file --batch` per package. It now runs one `git log` for all manifests (`first_parent_commits_by_path` in `callisto-model`, using `--first-parent -m` and literal pathspecs) plus one batched read. A package whose newest candidate is not the version-setting commit falls back to its own read, so results are unchanged.\n- `workspace_package` rescanned every package and recomputed identities on each call. It is replaced by a map built once (`ReleaseOwners`), every call site is migrated, and per-selection linear scans are now set lookups.\n\nMeasured on a synthetic monorepo (1,800 packages, 1,500 depending on one core package, 1,000 pending changesets, 20,000 tags): `release --dry-run` 13.9 s to 1.85 s and 3,012 git processes to 14 (debug), 8.10 s to 1.27 s (release build). With 20,000 commits it goes from 7.95 s to 1.63 s, and `compose-pr-body` from 12.1 s to 1.45 s (debug) and 1.90 s to 0.76 s (release). `status`, `version --dry-run` and the other dimensions benchmarked flat or linear and are untouched.\n\n## Verify\n\nOld and new output are byte-identical for `release --dry-run` text and JSON and for `compose-pr-body` on both large cases.\n\nA counting-runner test pins one `git log` and a bounded `cat-file` count at 3 and at 12 packages, and two mutations fail it. A 3,000-package test fails if the index is rebuilt per lookup (18 s against 0.04 s); it is wall-clock based with about a 250x margin, so only a very loaded CI machine risks a flake. The existing version-commit tests, including a 105-edit and merge-commit cases, pass.\n\n`just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0. CI has not run.\n\nNot changed: `version --emit-preview` takes 33 to 45 s when thousands of packages are bumped, about 75% of it macOS `F_FULLFSYNC` from the per-file and per-directory fsync. That is the durability invariant in AGENTS.md, so it is left alone.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HUceBbrJyeVNpSFsB5hEdj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr edit 507 --title \"perf(release): plan a large release with a fixed number of git processes\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr507_final.md; gh pr list --state open --json number,title --jq '.[]|\"\\(.number) \\(.title)\"'","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"86246d07f707e6cf7137542a55cff2015f72d32b4c08049d7c651db257434c1a","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DCdA2xe6Qj64GNMuEmRrPx","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr507_final.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HUceBbrJyeVNpSFsB5hEdj","type":"tool_result","content":"ok edited #507\n507 perf(release): plan a large release with a fixed number of git processes\n506 fix(errors): give each invalid callisto.toml value its own code\n505 test: assert every json success output carries a schemaVersion\n504 test: pin stability contracts for tags, action inputs, exit codes and config\n495 docs: clarify changeset authoring scope and timing\n493 chore(release): version packages","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"d064916a-ff1f-40fa-ba9b-2bf63b9535f5","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:59:41.969Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"a5d78a38c3b33787e5b5d9b7008e9de2db1c7b9a9ca69bf894342b554f4e1149","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"e2ee415a-04bd-47b5-b884-87ca29b0026a","keep":1544,"tail":["308d07fe8001e7115474cab4bef9971b9ee30386529fe5c5a2a24e2902d05a63","86246d07f707e6cf7137542a55cff2015f72d32b4c08049d7c651db257434c1a","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1546,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"56be5994fb309b42e6691e3a4b6e6b69ea3ef5c076ae1c0fb0323319acb0cd1d"}
{"parentUuid":"29b74c96-835d-4b9a-a902-43c0ad25f09a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwVofcZTYohiaErZ6K4w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #507 now has its description, and all four PRs for the next release have theirs. No agents are running, so everything I can do on this batch is done.\n\n**Open and waiting on your review**\n- **#504:** contract tests for tag names, Action inputs, exit codes and unknown config keys.\n- **#505:** the `schemaVersion` test for every JSON output.\n- **#506:** E254 retired, E330 to E339 added.\n- **#507:** the release-path performance fixes.\n- **#495:** the changeset process docs.\n\n#493, the 0.20.0 release PR, is waiting on those.\n\n**What 0.20.0 will contain, user-facing**\n- **Breaking, with notes:** camelCase JSON keys, exit 2 for usage errors, and error-code meanings (E111, E171, E254, and the new E3xx).\n- **Behavior:** unknown group keys rejected, `pre enter` validates tags, `add` rejects duplicate packages, and `status` JSON has stable fields.\n- **Fast:** large-monorepo release planning from about 8 s to 1.3 s, and the unreleased-changes check from 151 git diffs to 4.\n- **Clearer:** the versioned-not-published line, private workspace roots skipped, and did-you-mean for packages.\n\n**Still waiting on a decision from you**\n1. The two small E165 help changes (yes or no).\n2. Whether to look at the macOS fsync cost in `version --emit-preview`, which the agent left alone because of the durability invariant.\n\nWhen the five PRs merge and #493 refreshes, I'll render the release PR and read it as a user before you merge it.\n\nneeds input: review and merge #504 to #507 and #495, then tell me, and I'll read #493."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1553,"cache_read_input_tokens":930466,"output_tokens":568,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1553,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":930466,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1553},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8d1b6068-7209-468f-a73c-ce433da03a47","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwVofCzNmZjE8nc6qWYC","requestRef":"d064916a-ff1f-40fa-ba9b-2bf63b9535f5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e78ff00d-c468-4251-b744-77712b15a339","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:59:46.949Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
