{"parentUuid":"180efb38-2c9b-4987-a45c-e09f73fe01ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZAivR3z2cu2iK3Bj1K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2092,"cache_read_input_tokens":932674,"output_tokens":2073,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1312},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2092,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2073,"cache_read_input_tokens":932674,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2092},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":15472,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"b35822e5-8d85-428a-ba71-50a7fc6fc88f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwZAicZPwwVc86fMTvhr","requestRef":"27a3a376-f6d1-4eb7-a6f9-0e6a38a8d03c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5b4f3cf7-d4d1-42dd-bf1b-bff90bc85932","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:44:04.453Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5e465e9b44611fbd","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"5b4f3cf7-d4d1-42dd-bf1b-bff90bc85932","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZAivR3z2cu2iK3Bj1K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixed. Most of #504 follows the idiomatic pattern, but two pieces don't, and I'd change both.\n\n**What's fine.** The tag-name, exit-code and config tests are ordinary Rust integration tests: they run the real binary against temp workspaces and assert on observable output. That's the right shape.\n\n**1. Pinning the Action inputs with a shell script and `.txt` lists: not the best choice.**\n- It follows the existing `.github/tests/*.sh` convention, so it's consistent. But those scripts exist to test shell and workflow behavior, and this one just compares data.\n- A Rust test is already possible with what's in the tree:\n  - `yaml-rust2` is already a workspace dependency of `callisto-graph`.\n  - `insta` (snapshot testing) is already a dev-dependency.\n  - So the test would parse `action.yml`, snapshot each input's name, `required` and default, and review changes with `cargo insta review`.\n- Benefits:\n  - It runs in `just test` like everything else.\n  - It's cross-platform, with no bash quirks. The agent had to avoid process substitution because of the sandbox.\n  - Snapshots are the standard Rust way to pin a data shape.\n  - It's one tool, not two.\n- **Keep shell** for scripts that are themselves shell, such as the hold and release scripts.\n\n**2. The `deny_unknown_fields` guard that scans source text: I'd drop it.**\n- It's a source-grepping test. This repo deleted one in #488, and the same reasoning applies: it breaks on formatting and can't see structs outside `src/config`.\n- The existing runtime test already loads a typo'd key into 12 tables. A schema-based check would be the only semantic upgrade, and it would mean adding `JsonSchema` derives to every raw config struct, which is more than this is worth.\n\n**What I'd do:** convert #1 to a Rust test with an `insta` snapshot, delete the shell script and `.txt` files and the `justfile` line, and remove #2. That turns #504 into pure Rust tests, with no new dependencies beyond using `yaml-rust2` as a dev-dependency in the CLI crate.\n\nneeds input: say go, and I'll make that change on #504 (about an hour of agent time, with a mutation check on the snapshot)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2092,"cache_read_input_tokens":932674,"output_tokens":2073,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1312},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2092,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2073,"cache_read_input_tokens":932674,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2092},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b35822e5-8d85-428a-ba71-50a7fc6fc88f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwZAicZPwwVc86fMTvhr","requestRef":"27a3a376-f6d1-4eb7-a6f9-0e6a38a8d03c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d54d9616-288d-4859-bfdb-75a7eb85015c","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:44:04.880Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5e465e9b44611fbd","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
