{"parentUuid":"cf417420-c6f8-4fb7-bc97-8fce4950d78d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZJc58ok38mBxyKC2cX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":942600,"output_tokens":1061,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":307},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":942600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8233,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"47c435ad-4009-4da1-9e38-6ec09b7dadd7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwZJbioDZy9h6y7Kdm4o","requestRef":"7b8433c5-4082-40b2-ba42-f3135960d8be","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a00aa6c4-4968-45b1-a973-055cd9a870eb","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:45:44.080Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"a00aa6c4-4968-45b1-a973-055cd9a870eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZJc58ok38mBxyKC2cX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not the best design. The test works, but it mostly checks something the compiler could guarantee, so I'd restructure it.\n\n**What I found in the code**\n- There is already a typed emit path: `emit_report<R: Report>`, where the `Report` trait requires a `schema_version()`. 25 call sites use it, so any report built that way can't omit `schemaVersion` and still compile.\n- The untyped `write_json` is still public and has exactly two production callers: the error report in `main.rs`, and `release inspect`, which prints a raw document.\n- So the 21-invocation test, which takes about 11 s, mostly re-checks what the type system already enforces. It only earns its keep for the escape hatches.\n\n**The more idiomatic, higher-value shape**\n1. **Close the escape hatch.** Make `write_json` private to the output module, and give `release inspect` an explicit `emit_document` function for its raw passthrough. Then a new command with a hand-built `json!` output no longer compiles, so a new command can't skip the envelope.\n2. **Compile-time exhaustiveness instead of a clap-tree walk and string allow-list.** Add a function that `match`es the command enum with no wildcard arm and returns each command's JSON contract (`Report`, `Document` or `NotJson`). Adding a command then forces a decision at compile time, not at test time.\n3. **Keep a small runtime smoke test** for what types can't see: stdout is valid JSON, and `command` and `dryRun` carry the right values. A dozen invocations are plenty.\n4. **Optionally** use `insta` snapshots for output shapes you want pinned in full, not just `schemaVersion`. That's the standard Rust tool and it's already a dev-dependency.\n\n**Net effect:** the contract moves from a slow, string-matched test to the type system, with a thin test for the remainder. #505 stays correct as it is today, so this is a quality upgrade and not a blocker.\n\nI'd bundle it with the #504 conversion I proposed earlier (Action inputs to a Rust snapshot test, drop the source-grepping guard). Both are one idea: **prefer types and Rust-native tests over shell, text scans and string lists.**\n\nneeds input: say go, and I'll make both changes, #504 and #505, with agents and mutation checks."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":942600,"output_tokens":1061,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":307},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":942600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"47c435ad-4009-4da1-9e38-6ec09b7dadd7","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwZJbioDZy9h6y7Kdm4o","requestRef":"7b8433c5-4082-40b2-ba42-f3135960d8be","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"21696ebd-0714-43e0-87ae-e14fb6c4e8c7","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:45:44.542Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
