{"parentUuid":"3dc6e47c-3df9-415b-b8fa-ce8c6393e809","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZXf6ZtuQPX6KSiYKC4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FW6qejf3chomYTbeaTe2nA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cargo build -p callisto-cli --all-targets 2>&1 | tail -3; echo \"exit: $?\"","timeout":900000,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2541,"cache_read_input_tokens":948560,"output_tokens":2612,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1651},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2541,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2612,"cache_read_input_tokens":948560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2541},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FW6qejf3chomYTbeaTe2nA":{"command":"cargo build -p callisto-cli --all-targets 2>&1 | tail -3; echo \"exit: $?\"","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true,"timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"22e32aec-cc90-451c-983e-afa1f5faa2e2","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwZXejjczsZK812egZnU","requestRef":"76cc3b11-c9e0-4448-8c6e-bce022f0a6b8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"48aa969f-bea0-4a22-ad2a-6a8418b16ec8","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:48:49.095Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"48aa969f-bea0-4a22-ad2a-6a8418b16ec8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZXf6ZtuQPX6KSiYKC4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TTeXkVFXuXnyxdWZbi9Ce8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/feedback_rust_types_not_tests_lean.md","content":"---\nname: rust-types-not-tests-lean\ndescription: Prefer compiler-enforced structure over tests, shell, text scans and string lists; delete before adding; no speculative generality. User called out over-engineering in the 0.20 stability batch.\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nIn Rust, enforce invariants with types (a trait bound, a private constructor, an exhaustive `match`) so the compiler checks them. A test is the fallback for what types cannot see, and it should be small.\n\n**Why:** In the 0.20 stability batch (2026-11-11) I let implementer agents add shell scripts plus text files to pin Action inputs, a source-text scan for `deny_unknown_fields`, a 21-invocation binary test for `schemaVersion` that the `Report` trait already guaranteed, a 233-code string list to classify exit codes, a Windows-length pathspec budget for an unsupported platform, and 15 new error codes (each a permanent frozen API). The user said \"you're not thinking in the rust way and you're over-engineering way too much\". The repo had already deleted a source-grepping test (#488).\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Before adding a test, ask whether a type or a private function makes the bug unrepresentable; do that instead. Reuse what is already in the tree (`insta`, `yaml-rust2`, `emit_report`/`Report`) rather than shell or text files.\n- No source-text scanning tests, no hand-maintained lists of strings that mirror code, no wall-clock assertions (count calls instead).\n- No code for unsupported platforms or hypothetical limits (docs/stability.md says Windows is unsupported).\n- Every new public surface (an error code, a JSON key, a flag) is permanent after 1.0: prefer fewer, broader ones.\n- Put \"prefer types, delete before adding, no speculative generality\" in every implementer brief, and review agent output for these before pushing.\n\nRelated: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]], [[feedback_measure_value_before_building]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2541,"cache_read_input_tokens":948560,"output_tokens":2612,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1651},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2541,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2612,"cache_read_input_tokens":948560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2541},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TTeXkVFXuXnyxdWZbi9Ce8":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/feedback_rust_types_not_tests_lean.md","content":"---\nname: rust-types-not-tests-lean\ndescription: Prefer compiler-enforced structure over tests, shell, text scans and string lists; delete before adding; no speculative generality. User called out over-engineering in the 0.20 stability batch.\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nIn Rust, enforce invariants with types (a trait bound, a private constructor, an exhaustive `match`) so the compiler checks them. A test is the fallback for what types cannot see, and it should be small.\n\n**Why:** In the 0.20 stability batch (2026-11-11) I let implementer agents add shell scripts plus text files to pin Action inputs, a source-text scan for `deny_unknown_fields`, a 21-invocation binary test for `schemaVersion` that the `Report` trait already guaranteed, a 233-code string list to classify exit codes, a Windows-length pathspec budget for an unsupported platform, and 15 new error codes (each a permanent frozen API). The user said \"you're not thinking in the rust way and you're over-engineering way too much\". The repo had already deleted a source-grepping test (#488).\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Before adding a test, ask whether a type or a private function makes the bug unrepresentable; do that instead. Reuse what is already in the tree (`insta`, `yaml-rust2`, `emit_report`/`Report`) rather than shell or text files.\n- No source-text scanning tests, no hand-maintained lists of strings that mirror code, no wall-clock assertions (count calls instead).\n- No code for unsupported platforms or hypothetical limits (docs/stability.md says Windows is unsupported).\n- Every new public surface (an error code, a JSON key, a flag) is permanent after 1.0: prefer fewer, broader ones.\n- Put \"prefer types, delete before adding, no speculative generality\" in every implementer brief, and review agent output for these before pushing.\n\nRelated: [[feedback_no_overengineering_confirm_intent]], [[feedback_measure_value_before_building]].\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"22e32aec-cc90-451c-983e-afa1f5faa2e2","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgwZXejjczsZK812egZnU","requestRef":"76cc3b11-c9e0-4448-8c6e-bce022f0a6b8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9ebb59c0-c965-4160-a05e-da2cb0db5d50","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:48:54.462Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug"