{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","id":"5ea004a3-4564-4c15-819b-6e3c46cdb858","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:49:05.277Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"a5d78a38c3b33787e5b5d9b7008e9de2db1c7b9a9ca69bf894342b554f4e1149","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"8852141b-52fe-488e-896b-d06a960bff7e","keep":1589,"tail":["00f604797eab6b994e539de76f9a86be27cbaa5ffcc217fa910023bd75043e44","e6c3481842f414c1b2e63a0386488c969606da2be3a54e168a17c976f1b4bdad","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1591,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"b2cff289f8ced35d9ab6c8691ab746896458f3509e8ee23aea1f092405c4f39d"}
{"parentUuid":"a5bbacec-53e1-4fdc-9fcb-9f16a2428c91","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01YUom1aaaNeRq8pmcFqJ2YE","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0b54690a-b30d-4065-9058-c820c7cc40e1","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:49:14.362Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"0b54690a-b30d-4065-9058-c820c7cc40e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZa6wsi4FsD3f4DQPYm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The lean #505 change builds clean, and I saved your principle to memory. Here's an honest sweep of where we're making the same mistake, based on what's actually in the merged and open PRs.\n\n**In the code and tests (the same root mistake: strings and scans where types belong)**\n1. **Exit-code classification (#502, merged).** It's a hand-maintained `USAGE_CODES` list plus a 233-code `RUNTIME_CODES` string in a test, matched against error-code strings. That's stringly-typed, and it's what turned main red twice when new codes arrived. The Rust way: the error variant itself says it's a usage error, for example a `Usage(..)` wrapper or an exhaustive `match` on the variant, and the exit code follows from the type. No list, and no classification test.\n2. **Fifteen new error codes (E325 to E339).** Every code is permanent API after 1.0, and nine of them (E330 to E338) differ only by which config key was wrong. A single \"invalid value for `<key>`\" code with the key in the message would do the same job with a fraction of the frozen surface, and it needs one test, not ten.\n3. **Pathspec chunking in #494, which I wrote.** It's a 24,000-byte budget justified by Windows' 32 KB command-line limit, but `docs/stability.md` says Windows is unsupported. That's speculative generality: code and a test for a platform we don't ship. I'd delete it.\n4. **`note_once` (#496).** A process-global `static Mutex<BTreeSet>` to dedupe notes. The type-driven version collects notes into the returned structure and prints once at the end. No global state.\n5. **A wall-clock assertion in #507** (\"3,000 packages under 10 s\"). The repo's pattern is counting calls with a recording runner, which doesn't flake. I'd replace it.\n6. **Still open and already covered above:** #504's shell and text-file input pin, #504's source-scanning guard, and #505's heavy table test.\n\n**In how I worked (the waste)**\n- **Agents were briefed to add tests, not to prefer types.** I never put \"prefer types, delete before adding\" in a brief, so each agent covered its bases with more machinery. The memory note fixes that for future briefs.\n- **Parallel PRs touching shared lists collided twice** (#500 and #502 on error codes, and the envelope test), costing two rework rounds and a red main. A type-based design removes the shared list that collided.\n- **Full verify on every tiny follow-up,** and a narrator agent per PR whose output I then rewrote, so I paid for each body twice.\n\n**What I'd do next, smallest first**\n1. Finish #505 lean (done locally: the heavy test is deleted and untyped JSON output is crate-private).\n2. Trim #504: drop the shell script, the text lists and the source-scan guard.\n3. Delete the Windows chunking and the wall-clock test.\n4. Replace the exit-code string lists with a type-based classification, if you want it before 1.0, since it also stops the collisions.\n\nneeds input: say go on 1 to 3 (I'll do them myself, no new agents), and tell me whether you want 4 and the code consolidation in 2 before 0.20.0."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":334,"cache_read_input_tokens":954819,"output_tokens":1060,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":334,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1060,"cache_read_input_tokens":954819,"cache_creation_input_tokens":334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":334},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnosti