{"parentUuid":"e1a0c708-a024-4d33-887a-6af699fb7e6e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZkSaMqLNCFN9oSRzG2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":958998,"output_tokens":3335,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1946},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":921,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3335,"cache_read_input_tokens":958998,"cache_creation_input_tokens":921,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":921},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":20432,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"a22a59d2-1f48-40ed-aaf7-59023895af39","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwZkS9ZB8RP6H3jbFrkZ","requestRef":"6afc410b-49a3-4121-ad37-2bc13c53d416","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"059a3651-39b0-4229-8b4a-5a460efc3480","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:51:46.887Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"059a3651-39b0-4229-8b4a-5a460efc3480","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZkSaMqLNCFN9oSRzG2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The best change is to put the preference in three places, and none of them need a long document: a short section in Callisto's AGENTS.md, a few clippy lints (so the compiler enforces it), and one authoring reference for the plugin agents.\n\n**What exists today, and the gap**\n- **Callisto AGENTS.md:** has \"safe Rust only\" and \"user-facing errors derive `miette::Diagnostic`\", but nothing about preferring types over tests, nothing about which crates to reuse, and no ban on text-scan tests or shell. That gap is why the agents added test machinery.\n- **Plugin references** (`shared/references/{architecture,verification,hazards}/rust.md`): `architecture/rust.md` is a smell *finder*, though it does list \"a rule that exists only in prose with no type, test or lint\". `verification/rust.md` lists test tools and says nothing about preferring a type to a test. There's no *authoring* guidance for `smith:implementer`, so it defaults to adding tests.\n\n**1. Callisto AGENTS.md: about 10 lines, no more**\n- Make illegal states unrepresentable: enums over flag combinations, newtypes for ids and paths, validating `FromStr`/`TryFrom`, private constructors, and an exhaustive `match` on our own enums with no `_` arm.\n- Share behavior with a trait and a generic bound, as `Report` and `emit_report` already do, instead of copying code or testing each copy.\n- Reuse the crate already in the tree: `thiserror` and `miette` for errors, `clap` derive for the CLI, `serde` (with `deny_unknown_fields` and `rename_all`), `tempfile`, `insta` for snapshots, `proptest` for properties, `rstest` for cases, and `schemars`. Add a dependency only when none fits. There is no async runtime, because this CLI is synchronous.\n- A test is the last resort for what types can't see. Never write a source-text scan, a shell script where Rust works, a string list that mirrors code, or a wall-clock assertion (count calls instead). No code for platforms we don't support.\n- Delete before adding. Every error code, JSON key and flag is permanent after 1.0, so add the fewest.\n\n**2. Lints, so the compiler says it for us (a few lines in `clippy.toml` and `[workspace.lints]`)**\n- `clippy::wildcard_enum_match_arm` forces exhaustive matches on our enums.\n- `clippy::disallowed_macros` on `serde_json::json!` in command modules makes a hand-built JSON envelope fail the build, replacing the 21-invocation test I deleted.\n- `clippy::print_stdout` and `print_stderr` force all output through `emit_report` and the output helpers.\n- Keep it to these. Each lint gets an explicit allow where we really need an exception.\n\n**3. Plugin repo: one new file and two sentences**\n- Add `shared/references/authoring/rust.md`, about 40 lines. It has the same ladder (type, then trait, then a small test), and a rule to **discover what the repo already depends on and reuse it, proposing a new crate only when none exists and saying why**. That keeps it correct across repos: tokio is right for an async service and wrong here.\n- Load it from `smith:implementer`'s `<load_first>`.\n- Add one row to `verification/rust.md`: \"an invariant a type can enforce: make it unrepresentable, test only the remainder\".\n- Add two failure modes to the implementer's `<judgment>`: \"adds a test, script or list that mirrors what a type could enforce\", and \"adds code for unsupported platforms or hypothetical limits\".\n\n**What I'd leave out.** A long Rust style guide (it wouldn't be read), and a per-crate rulebook in the global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, which is shared across languages.\n\n**Who does what.** I can make 1 and 2 in Callisto now, as one small PR with no new dependencies. The plugin edits in 3 belong in the repo you're already working in, so I'll give you the exact text rather than edit it myself.\n\nneeds input: say go and I'll do 1 and 2 in Callisto, and send you the plugin text for 3."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":958998,"output_tokens":3335,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1946},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":921,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3335,"cache_read_input_tokens":958998,"cache_creation_input_tokens":921,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":921},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a22a59d2-1f48-40ed-aaf7-59023895af39","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwZkS9ZB8RP6H3jbFrkZ","requestRef":"6afc410b-49a3-4121-ad37-2bc13c53d416","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"44d9bd12-989a-4352-8767-b1f24be7bdbd","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:51:51.609Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"44d9bd12-989a-4352-8767-b1f24be7bdbd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"75f4a572-952f-4972-a6ac-36fbfb333166","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stop\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4\\\",\\\"query\\\":\\\"What can we change about rust guidance to prefer types, traits, usage of common crates for specific cases (like tokio, miete, etc)\\\",\\\"response\\\":\\\"The best change is to put the preference in three places, and none of them need a long document: a short section in Callisto's AGENTS.md, a few clippy lints (so the compiler enforces it), and one a...\\\",\\\"transcript_path\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto--claude-worktrees-agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8.jsonl\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-stop.sh","durationMs":1190},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1fea641c-dca6-4c2c-bc3c-8a1b6cb27ab3","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:51:52.842Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
