{"parentUuid":"a50c5df7-c224-4a13-9a91-edd5ce2fc33d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZwtimyennVs56q4ogx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Launching two read-only bug-hunters in parallel: one for over-engineering (the prompt above, condensed) and one for real defects in the 0.20 batch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50631,"cache_read_input_tokens":29508,"output_tokens":2439,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":353},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50631,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2439,"cache_read_input_tokens":29508,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50631},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"system_changed","cache_missed_input_tokens":47466}},"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3c9fd3aa-e808-42a0-bb44-2292fc752203","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwZwtRRQke38jbjxqtQj","requestRef":"dad44e9c-0931-4674-9e6d-99cced6e65f8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7c2264f6-b847-40a6-a251-c882e5e43c34","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:54:04.990Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"7c2264f6-b847-40a6-a251-c882e5e43c34","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZwtimyennVs56q4ogx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HPUihTetMbTzvrU6G9JhCv","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Over-engineering audit","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only audit of /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4 (Callisto, a synchronous Rust release CLI, no async). Do not edit. Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first. Do not run the full test suite.\n\nPrinciple: enforce invariants with types, traits and exhaustive matches; tests are the small fallback. Delete before adding. Every public surface (error code, JSON key, flag) is permanent after 1.0. Windows is unsupported.\n\nFind, with file:line and counts:\n1. Stringly-typed classification: hand-maintained string lists mirroring code (USAGE_CODES, RUNTIME_CODES in crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs), matching on code() strings.\n2. Tests re-checking what a type/trait bound already guarantees.\n3. Source-text scanning tests (include_str!/read_to_string of src then string search).\n4. Shell scripts / .txt fixtures (.github/tests, justfile) where Rust (insta, yaml-rust2, toml, serde_json) would do.\n5. Speculative generality: unsupported-platform code (e.g. PATHSPEC_BUDGET/list_in_chunks in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs), one-caller parameters, traits with one implementor and no test double.\n6. Global mutable state (static Mutex/OnceLock, e.g. note_once in crates/callisto-graph/src/note.rs).\n7. Wall-clock assertions in tests (repo pattern is call counting).\n8. Duplicated mappings / near-identical tests collapsible with rstest or a helper.\n9. Permanent surface that could be broader: count error codes, JSON keys, flags per area; nine near-identical config error codes (E330-E339 area).\n10. Wildcard arms on own enums, bool flag soup, Option fields valid only together, String where a newtype belongs.\n11. Reinvented functionality where a crate already in Cargo.lock fits (do not propose new deps).\n\nNot findings: tests driving the real binary for observable behavior; anything required by docs/stability.md; durability/security invariants in AGENTS.md (atomic writes with fsync); anything you cannot show is reachable or duplicated (read callers).\n\nReport: ranked by value of removal. Per finding: pattern #, file:line, instance count, evidence, lean replacement (one or two sentences), risk and whether it touches a frozen 1.0 surface, confidence. End with the top five changes and patterns you looked for and did not find. Under 800 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50631,"cache_read_input_tokens":29508,"output_tokens":2439,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":353},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50631,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2439,"cache_read_input_tokens":29508,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50631},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"system_changed","cache_missed_input_tokens":47466}},"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HPUihTetMbTzvrU6G9JhCv":{"description":"Over-engineering audit","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only audit of /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4 (Callisto, a synchronous Rust release CLI, no async). Do not edit. Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first. Do not run the full test suite.\n\nPrinciple: enforce invariants with types, traits and exhaustive matches; tests are the small fallback. Delete before adding. Every public surface (error code, JSON key, flag) is permanent after 1.0. Windows is unsupported.\n\nFind, with file:line and counts:\n1. Stringly-typed classification: hand-maintained string lists mirroring code (USAGE_CODES, RUNTIME_CODES in crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs), matching on code() strings.\n2. Tests re-checking what a type/trait bound already guarantees.\n3. Source-text scanning tests (include_str!/read_to_string of src then string search).\n4. Shell scripts / .txt fixtures (.github/tests, justfile) where Rust (insta, yaml-rust2, toml, serde_json) would do.\n5. Speculative generality: unsupported-platform code (e.g. PATHSPEC_BUDGET/list_in_chunks in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs), one-caller parameters, traits with one implementor and no test double.\n6. Global mutable state (static Mutex/OnceLock, e.g. note_once in crates/callisto-graph/src/note.rs).\n7. Wall-clock assertions in tests (repo pattern is call counting).\n8. Duplicated mappings / near-identical tests collapsible with rstest or a helper.\n9. Permanent surface that could be broader: count error codes, JSON keys, flags per area; nine near-identical config error codes (E330-E339 area).\n10. Wildcard arms on own enums, bool flag soup, Option fields valid only together, String where a newtype belongs.\n11. Reinvented functionality where a crate already in Cargo.lock fits (do not propose new deps).\n\nNot findings: tests driving the real binary for observable behavior; anything required by docs/stability.md; durability/security invariants in AGENTS.md (atomic writes with fsync); anything you cannot show is reachable or duplicated (read callers).\n\nReport: ranked by value of removal. Per finding: pattern #, file:line, instance count, evidence, lean replacement (one or two sentences), risk and whether it touches a frozen 1.0 surface, confidence. End with the top five changes and patterns you looked for and did not find. Under 800 words."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3c9fd3aa-e808-42a0-bb44-2292fc752203","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwZwtRRQke38jbjxqtQj","requestRef":"dad44e9c-0931-4674-9e6d-99cced6e65f8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"869cfdf3-ee9a-4059-b911-3bd79b8011a3","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:54:11.621Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"869cfdf3-ee9a-4059-b911-3bd79b8011a3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZwtimyennVs56q4ogx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011hUPSkVWUxRj5PRemvZ6v2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Bug hunt 0.20 batch","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only adversarial bug hunt in /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4 (Callisto, Rust release CLI). Do not edit. Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first. You may run narrow `cargo test -p <crate> <filter>` or the binary against temp repos; do not run the full suite. Report only defects you can demonstrate from code or a run.\n\nScope: code added or changed in the recent 0.20 stability and performance batch (see `git log -40 --stat` on this branch and origin/main):\n- Exit codes: USAGE_CODES / USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES and CliError::is_usage_error in crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs, main.rs exit mapping; promise in docs/stability.md is 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage. Look for error codes mapped to the wrong exit code, or codes missing from docs/errors.md or reused.\n- JSON contract: emit_report/Report envelope (schemaVersion, command, dryRun), write_document / write_error_json in crates/callisto-cli/src/output.rs; any command that prints JSON outside the envelope, snake_case keys leaking, error envelope on stderr vs stdout consistency.\n- Config validation: unknown-key rejection (deny_unknown_fields), E325 UnknownField, E326 InvalidValue, tag/prerelease validation in crates/callisto-graph/src/config/resolve.rs; inputs that are wrongly rejected (dotted pre tags like beta.1 must work) or wrongly accepted.\n- Performance changes: crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs (one git diff per tag commit, pathspec chunking), crates/callisto-model/src/vcs/access.rs first_parent_commits_by_path (git log --first-parent -m -z --name-only --relative), Releas