{"parentUuid":"869cfdf3-ee9a-4059-b911-3bd79b8011a3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d63a3721-2a40-4bbf-88c4-736158ed03ba","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HPUihTetMbTzvrU6G9JhCv","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a84cbea4ce07ea1ea (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a84cbea4ce07ea1ea', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a84cbea4ce07ea1ea.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"a0e302a8-509e-498a-8f24-392bf8846da2","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:54:18.443Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a84cbea4ce07ea1ea","description":"Over-engineering audit","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Read-only audit of /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4 (Callisto, a synchronous Rust release CLI, no async). Do not edit. Read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md first. Do not run the full test suite.\n\nPrinciple: enforce invariants with types, traits and exhaustive matches; tests are the small fallback. Delete before adding. Every public surface (error code, JSON key, flag) is permanent after 1.0. Windows is unsupported.\n\nFind, with file:line and counts:\n1. Stringly-typed classification: hand-maintained string lists mirroring code (USAGE_CODES, RUNTIME_CODES in crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs), matching on code() strings.\n2. Tests re-checking what a type/trait bound already guarantees.\n3. Source-text scanning tests (include_str!/read_to_string of src then string search).\n4. Shell scripts / .txt fixtures (.github/tests, justfile) where Rust (insta, yaml-rust2, toml, serde_json) would do.\n5. Speculative generality: unsupported-platform code (e.g. PATHSPEC_BUDGET/list_in_chunks in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs), one-caller parameters, traits with one implementor and no test double.\n6. Global mutable state (static Mutex/OnceLock, e.g. note_once in crates/callisto-graph/src/note.rs).\n7. Wall-clock assertions in tests (repo pattern is call counting).\n8. Duplicated mappings / near-identical tests collapsible with rstest or a helper.\n9. Permanent surface that could be broader: count error codes, JSON keys, flags per area; nine near-identical config error codes (E330-E339 area).\n10. Wildcard arms on own enums, bool flag soup, Option fields valid only together, String where a newtype belongs.\n11. Reinvented functionality where a crate already in Cargo.lock fits (do not propose new deps).\n\nNot findings: tests driving the real binary for observable behavior; anything required by docs/stability.md; durability/security invariants in AGENTS.md (atomic writes with fsync); anything you cannot show is reachable or duplicated (read callers).\n\nReport: ranked by value of removal. Per finding: pattern #, file:line, instance count, evidence, lean replacement (one or two sentences), risk and whether it touches a frozen 1.0 surface, confidence. End with the top five changes and patterns you looked for and did not find. Under 800 words.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-ca