{"parentUuid":"6b4b8c98-4cda-4101-98d0-fb3fa58a11d5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwaNML6VD6mbUoAPMeTj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5954,"cache_read_input_tokens":100017,"output_tokens":3741,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2317},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5954,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3741,"cache_read_input_tokens":100017,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5954},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":24318,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"dbff75c6-db27-4013-9a21-0259af4a0b78","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwaNM5xTHkazW7FoninL","requestRef":"b10ce4a7-a5e9-4a53-bf52-95a03c640b2b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2182221c-9b7f-4968-928d-54e3b94ca9cd","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:59:57.577Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"2182221c-9b7f-4968-928d-54e3b94ca9cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwaNML6VD6mbUoAPMeTj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked findings 1, 2, 5, 6 and 7 and both bugs against the code. Findings 3, 4, 8 and 9 are taken from the auditor's report and are still unchecked.\n\n**What held up**\n- **Credential lists (1):** there are five copies, two already differ (`NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG` versus `CALLISTO_PUBLISH_NPM_CONFIG`), and three tests exist only to cross-check them. A leak is unproven: it depends on whether `CALLISTO_PUBLISH_NPM_CONFIG` is set in a build backend's environment, which I haven't traced.\n- **Exit codes (2):** `USAGE_CODES` and a 230-code `RUNTIME_CODES` string cover 274 `#[diagnostic(code(E…))]` attributes. Runtime is the default, so only the usage variants need naming, in one exhaustive `exit_kind()` match per error type with `_ => Runtime`. That deletes `RUNTIME_CODES` and its meta-test.\n- **Wall-clock asserts (5):** `runner.rs` has five. **Global state (7):** `note_once` has 8 call sites.\n- **Chunking (6):** the budget is real code for Windows. A better fix than deleting it is possible: `changed.rs` already has `SpecIndex`, which maps paths to owning packages. One unscoped `git diff --name-only` per tag commit mapped through it needs no pathspecs, no budget and no argument limit. That needs a small design check for the ignore excludes.\n\n**Reinvented problems and crates**\n- **Prerelease grammar:** the `pre enter 01` bug exists because `validate_tag` hand-writes the SemVer identifier rules. `semver` is already a workspace dependency, and `semver::Prerelease::new` rejects `01`, so parsing with it removes the bug and the code. The non-dotted snapshot-tag rule is a different grammar and stays.\n- **Subprocess runner:** `runner.rs` hand-rolls a deadline loop with output capping. `wait-timeout` and `duct` exist, but I haven't compared them. The pipe-draining past the cap is the delicate part, so this is worth a look and not a recommendation.\n- **Workflow checks:** from memory, `actionlint` and `zizmor` cover GitHub Actions policy better than our `rg` scripts. I haven't checked their fit, and you've already questioned how strict those checks should be.\n- **Not a crate problem:** `miette` and `thiserror` can't carry an exit kind, so the exhaustive match is the right tool. `secrecy` and `zeroize` protect values in memory and don't help with lists of env names. Shelling out to git is defensible, so I wouldn't move to `gix`.\n\n**Root causes**\n1. **No `ErrorCode` type.** The E-number is the identity, spread over the `#[diagnostic]` attributes, `docs/errors.md` and test strings, so every per-code fact (exit kind, documented, unique) becomes a string join with a test guarding it.\n2. **Tests used as the invariant mechanism.** The ladder should be: type, then exhaustive match, then clippy lint, then one small test. Duplicated lists need extra tests to keep them aligned, which is why the cross-check tests exist.\n3. **Hand-written grammars where a crate already is the spec.** `semver::Prerelease` is the case here.\n\n`docs/architecture` is prose only, with no machine-readable model, and Brain has no memory covering these decisions.\n\n**Proposed order, each a small PR off `origin/main` in its own worktree**\n1. Bug fixes: `rev:./dir` for `changedSinceLastTag`, and `Prerelease::new` for `pre enter`.\n2. One credential table in `callisto-model`, with the duplicates and cross-check tests deleted.\n3. `exit_kind()`, plus the deletions of the wall-clock asserts and the auto-traits test.\n4. The `SpecIndex` rewrite of the chunking.\n5. An \"invariant ladder\" section in `AGENTS.md`, plus one Brain memory.\n\nneeds input: say go (or reorder or skip items) and I'll start PRs 1 and 2 in parallel."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5954,"cache_read_input_tokens":100017,"output_tokens":3741,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2317},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5954,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3741,"cache_read_input_tokens":100017,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5954},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dbff75c6-db27-4013-9a21-0259af4a0b78","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwaNM5xTHkazW7FoninL","requestRef":"b10ce4a7-a5e9-4a53-bf52-95a03c640b2b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f24b9ffb-fe7a-4c91-93d2-563a6881772b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:00:01.972Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
