{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"871034728bd759dc810d8094a3f516b340b591800f559f5f075db9eb3da1eb4c","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012fJfnnGbpXUfpvoZpqnoxH","type":"tool_result","content":"assets/\ncrates/\ndocs/\nevals/\nfuzz/\npackages/\nscripts/\nAGENTS.md  6.3K\nARCHITECTURE.md  7.4K\nCHANGELOG.md  2.2K\nCLAUDE.md  134B\nCODE_OF_CONDUCT.md  5.1K\nCONTRIBUTING.md  8.7K\nCargo.lock  27.2K\nCargo.toml  2.6K\nLICENSE  1.0K\nPRINCIPLES.md  9.1K\nREADME.md  9.2K\nSECURITY.md  3.3K\ncallisto.toml  1.3K\ndeny.toml  835B\njustfile  8.2K\nmoon.yml  1.2K\npackage.json  356B\npnpm-lock.yaml  7.7K\nrust-toolchain.toml  77B\n... (2 filtered)\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/orin-dx/michi/main/assets/brand/hero-dark.png\">\n    <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/orin-dx/michi/main/assets/brand/hero-light.png\" alt=\"michi, an Orin DX tool\" width=\"360\">\n  </picture>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">道</p>\n\n[![CI](https://github.com/orin-dx/michi/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/orin-dx/michi/actions/workflows/ci.yml) [![License: FSL-1.1-MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-FS\n\nAXI response primitives for agent-ergonomic tools — TOON lists, key-value blocks, truncation, structured errors, status, and `help[]` hints.\n\n`michi` is the formatting and response layer for the [Orin DX](https://orin-dx.com) tools: it turns structured data into token-efficient, agent-readable text. No CLI framework or async runtime require\n\nAvailable as Rust crates (`michi-core`, plus `michi-pipeline` for async execution and the MIT `michi-graph` for dependency graphs) or a Node.js package (`@orin-dx/michi`).\n\nFor developer docs, start with the [documentation map](https://github.com/orin-dx/michi/blob/main/docs/README.md). API reference: [michi-core](https://docs.rs/michi-core), [michi-pipeline](https://doc\n\n## Install\n\nRust:\n\n```bash\ncargo add michi-core\ncargo add michi-pipeline   # optional: async pipeline execution on Tokio\ncargo add michi-graph      # optional: dependency graphs (MIT, no dependencies)\n```\n\nNode.js:\n\n```bash\nnpm i @orin-dx/michi\n```\n\nThe npm package ships prebuilt native binaries for these platforms:\n\n- macOS on Apple silicon (`darwin-arm64`)\n- macOS on Intel (`darwin-x64`)\n- Linux x64 with glibc (`linux-x64-gnu`)\n9:| callisto-model | MIT | none (external: `michi-graph`, MIT) |\n15:- `callisto-model` (MIT) must never depend on an FSL crate. It depends on `michi-graph` (MIT, no dependencies of its own) for dependency-graph validation and ordering. `just license-boundary` fails if anything it builds with is FSL.\n1:[workspace]\n2:members  = [\n13:[workspace.package]\n23:[workspace.dependencies]\n61:[workspace.lints.rust]\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GGs9evKtaKMcJdeWSY8oGA","type":"tool_result","content":"crates/callisto-model/src/vcs/access.rs:1086:            let output = std::process::Command::new(program)\ncrates/callisto-model/src/vcs/access.rs:1107:        let status = std::process::Command::new(\"git\")\ncrates/callisto-cli/benches/commands.rs:64:    let output = Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_callisto\"))\ncrates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs:155:        let mut command = std::process::Command::new(program);\ncrates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs:299:        let mut command = std::process::Command::new(program);\ncrates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs:452:    let mut command = std::process::Command::new(program);\ncrates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs:739:        let output = std::process::Command::new(exe)\ncrates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs:954:        let output = std::process::Command::new(exe)\ncrates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs:1127:        let output = std::process::Command::new(exe)\ncrates/callist