{"parentUuid":"ceaf166f-9abf-4c1b-be69-b855966947f6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwaXWcTTt5nh7nQCviXx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3593,"cache_read_input_tokens":110920,"output_tokens":1923,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":959},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3593,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1923,"cache_read_input_tokens":110920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3593},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":12697,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"a3d2156d-424d-4ded-9d70-70fe26125836","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwaXWHrGHGJjTirsVmGv","requestRef":"f257974b-c098-4c3f-8363-ed63e4e2a2ad","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9d4037e8-2ab7-4937-ac40-94d0cf90fb7d","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:01:50.236Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"9d4037e8-2ab7-4937-ac40-94d0cf90fb7d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwaXWcTTt5nh7nQCviXx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Michi is the sibling Orin DX repo, the \"AXI response primitives\" layer. Callisto currently depends only on `michi-graph` (MIT, dependency graphs). I haven't read the rest of michi, so I can't say yet whether a subprocess runner belongs there.\n\n**On wait-timeout and duct**\n- They would replace only the 50 ms `try_wait` poll loop at `runner.rs:504`, about 15 lines. The output cap, secret redaction, reader threads, the bounded 3-second grace period and env filtering would all stay custom. The gain is small, so I wouldn't swap crates for it.\n- A shared runner would belong in michi only if another Orin tool needs the same behaviour. `michi-pipeline` is async on Tokio and Callisto is sync, and `michi-core` is FSL, which `callisto-model` (MIT) can't depend on.\n\n**What to dig into before a comprehensive plan**\n1. **Michi's contents.** Read `michi-core` and `michi-pipeline`. Michi advertises \"structured errors\", which may already be the typed error-code and exit-kind layer we lack. This is the biggest unknown.\n2. **Subprocess sites.** There are five `Command::new` production sites (`runner.rs` x3, `access.rs` x2) plus `version.rs`. List what each needs, then compare it with the crates and with michi.\n3. **Credential leak.** Trace the build and publish child environments to settle whether `CALLISTO_PUBLISH_NPM_CONFIG` can reach a build backend. That decides whether PR 2 is a security fix or a cleanup.\n4. **Exit kind.** Enumerate which error enums hold the 29 usage codes, and check `docs/stability.md` so the mapping stays byte-identical.\n5. **`changed.rs`.** Find out why the diff is pathspec-scoped, how `ignore` excludes would work after filtering in Rust, and benchmark an unscoped diff on the 1,800-package fixture.\n6. **Unchecked audit findings.** Verify findings 3, 4, 8 and 9, and check whether `zizmor` or `actionlint` fit the workflow-contract scripts.\n7. **Open-PR overlap.** Run `merge-tree` for #495, #504, #505, #506 and #507. #504 and #506 touch the same tests and codes, and #507 touches `ReleaseOwners`. The plan has to follow their merge order.\n8. **Cross-repo duplication.** Check whether moon, proto or caliper carry copies of the same patterns.\n\nItems 1, 2, 3 and 5 are the ones that change the plan. I'd run them as two read-only agents: one on michi and subprocess, and one on credentials, `changed.rs` and the PR overlap.\n\nneeds input: say go and I'll launch those two investigations (the bug fixes can proceed in parallel if you want)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3593,"cache_read_input_tokens":110920,"output_tokens":1923,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":959},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3593,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1923,"cache_read_input_tokens":110920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3593},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a3d2156d-424d-4ded-9d70-70fe26125836","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwaXWHrGHGJjTirsVmGv","requestRef":"f257974b-c098-4c3f-8363-ed63e4e2a2ad","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"be2dd69c-bbcd-4c43-b07f-dc159d3230fd","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:01:51.263Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoin