s pathspec-scoped? How are `ignore` excludes applied (exclude_pathspec)? Could one unscoped `git diff --name-only <commit>` per tag commit, mapped to packages via SpecIndex plus a Rust-side ignore filter (globset/ignore crates if already dependencies), give identical results? List semantics that would differ (ignore patterns, gitignored/untracked, submodules, --relative). Also note the `rev:dir` bug at lines 67-68 (git resolves rev:path from the repo top, not cwd; should be rev:./dir).\nD. Open PR overlap: for open PRs #495, #504, #505, #506, #507 on orin-dx/callisto (use `gh pr list` and `git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only origin/main origin/<branch>` pairwise), report which touch usage_exit_codes_tests.rs, error.rs, changed.rs, runner.rs, registry.rs and which pairs conflict, so a plan can order the work.\nUnder 800 words, ranked by how much each changes the plan."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52,"cache_read_input_tokens":125464,"output_tokens":2172,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":119},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2172,"cache_read_input_tokens":125464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014kVELbF7rVun4EX7NJkAq8":{"description":"Credentials, diff, PR overlap","subagent_type":"bug-hunter","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only investigation in /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4 (Callisto Rust release CLI). 