{"parentUuid":"30e92643-dbbe-499e-bfbe-1b28309223c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwb3LpvgFE2scr6T3Vuf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5353,"cache_read_input_tokens":134437,"output_tokens":1350,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":315},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5353,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1350,"cache_read_input_tokens":134437,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5353,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5353},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2781,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"6052744f-d05d-4308-88e2-0d09a9087582","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgwb3LYoe5utyuwoPhPcs","requestRef":"e851d957-7de0-48a2-a9b9-88232b6c57d6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"100e53f2-8ef0-41ad-9bd5-32ad2df38f3f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T18:08:24.982Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aafeb13134f6a0ae4","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/json-contract-complete","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"100e53f2-8ef0-41ad-9bd5-32ad2df38f3f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwb3LpvgFE2scr6T3Vuf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both investigations are done and I can give the plan. This is the second agent's report. I haven't re-run its traces, but they match what I read earlier.\n\n**What changed the plan**\n- **Credentials: no leak.** `CALLISTO_PUBLISH_NPM_CONFIG` can't reach a build backend, because the runner strips it from every child that doesn't own it. The lists differ, but their union is complete, and tests already enforce that every secret is redacted. A single table would need four flags, which is itself the over-engineering we're avoiding. I'd drop this or do it last, and only if it deletes more than it adds.\n- **`changed.rs`** already does one diff per tag commit and maps files back through `SpecIndex`. Only the pathspec scoping and the chunking remain. Replacing them with an unscoped diff plus a `globset` filter is feasible. Two caveats: the matcher needs `literal_separator(true)` to match git's glob behaviour, and `pkg[1]`-style directory names would match more correctly than today.\n- **`exit_kind()`** is clean. 26 of the 29 usage codes are `CliError` variants, 3 are `GraphError` (E195, E196, E324), and E316 and E317 are `ConfigError` variants that count only when the reference came from a `--` flag. `main.rs:35` is the only consumer.\n- **Open PRs** merge cleanly in every pair checked. Only #504 and #506 both edit `usage_exit_codes_tests.rs`, so `exit_kind()` should land after both and delete the list once. None of them touches `changed.rs`, `runner.rs` or the registry files.\n\n**Plan, each a small PR off `origin/main` in its own named worktree**\n1. **Bug fixes (start now):** `rev:./dir` in `changed.rs` and `semver::Prerelease` in `pre enter`, each with a regression test. The agent said to wait for #507, but the fix touches only `changed.rs`, so I don't see a reason to wait.\n2. **Land your open PRs first:** #495 and #505, then #504, #506 and #507, so I can build on them.\n3. **`exit_kind()`** after #504 and #506. It deletes `USAGE_CODES`, `RUNTIME_CODES` and the meta-test.\n4. **Deletions:** the wall-clock asserts, `test_auto_traits`, the source-text scan tests and the `snapshot.rs` `include_str!` test, once I've checked them myself.\n5. **`changed.rs`** unscoped diff plus `SpecIndex` and a `globset` filter, which removes `PATHSPEC_BUDGET` and `list_in_chunks`.\n6. **`note_once`** without the global.\n7. **`AGENTS.md`** invariant-ladder section and the Brain memory.\n8. **Optional:** the credential table and the workflow-script replacement.\n\nMichi contributes nothing to this. The only upstream candidate is the token-shape masker, and it waits for a second tool.\n\nI can start PR 1 now while you land the open PRs.\n\nneeds input: say go and I'll start the bug-fix PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5353,"cache_read_input_tokens":134437,"output_tokens":1350,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":315},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5353,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1350,"cache_read_input_tokens":134437,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5353,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5353},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6052744f-d05d-4308-88e2-0d09a9087582","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgwb3LYoe5utyuwoPhPcs","requestRef":"e851d957-7de0-48a2-a9b9-88232b6c57d6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a35374a9-05e1-418a-aca8-c824665947cf","t