{"parentUuid":"e05b9f98-93b0-471a-9412-7415d10e41cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwkwCFV5DpGynkZDHZRT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BeAq8NhLQ3BwjedNm7Y5aW","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"AGENTS.md invariant ladder section","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"low","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). First: read AGENTS.md fully. Then `git fetch origin` and `git switch -c docs/invariant-ladder origin/main`.\n\nHOUSE RULES: commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links; never hard-wrap prose (one line per paragraph); terse, plain, no AI slop. Verify by exit code with `just doc-check` and `just pre-push` (dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true if needed). Push (`git push -u origin docs/invariant-ladder`). Do NOT open a PR; no changeset.\n\nTASK: add ONE short section to AGENTS.md (match the file's heading style, place it near the existing testing/code-style guidance, at most 12 lines, no new top-level structure) titled for how to enforce an invariant. Content, in your own plain words, the ladder in order: (1) a type or a private constructor/field so the wrong thing cannot compile; (2) an exhaustive `match` with no `_` arm on our own enums; (3) a clippy/rustc lint already in workspace lints; (4) one small test that drives the real binary or function for observable behavior; (5) nothing. Then four rules: no tests that scan source text or grep docs/workflows for strings that code can expose directly; no hand-maintained lists of strings that mirror code (error codes, command names, env names) — derive from the type; prefer a crate already in Cargo.lock (semver for versions, miette/thiserror for errors, clap derive for args, serde for formats, insta for snapshots) over a hand-written grammar; every new error code, JSON key or flag is permanent after 1.0, so prefer fewer broader ones. One line on deletion: before adding a check, delete one that a type now covers. Do not edit anything else.\n\nREPORT (under 80 words): the diff size, commit signed?, doc-check and pre-push exit results."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9181,"cache_read_input_tokens":213738,"output_tokens":9867,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2986},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9181,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9867,"cache_read_input_tokens":213738,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9181},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BeAq8NhLQ3BwjedNm7Y5aW":{"description":"AGENTS.md invariant ladder section","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"low","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). First: read AGENTS.md fully. Then `git fetch origin` and `git switch -c docs/invariant-ladder origin/main`.\n\nHOUSE RULES: commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links; never hard-wrap prose (one line per paragraph); terse, plain, no AI slop. Verify by exit