laude.ai links; never hard-wrap prose (one line per paragraph); terse, plain, no AI slop. Verify by exit code with `just doc-check` and `just pre-push` (dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true if needed). Push (`git push -u origin docs/invariant-ladder`). Do NOT open a PR; no changeset.\n\nTASK: add ONE short section to AGENTS.md (match the file's heading style, place it near the existing testing/code-style guidance, at most 12 lines, no new top-level structure) titled for how to enforce an invariant. Content, in your own plain words, the ladder in order: (1) a type or a private constructor/field so the wrong thing cannot compile; (2) an exhaustive `match` with no `_` arm on our own enums; (3) a clippy/rustc lint already in workspace lints; (4) one small test that drives the real binary or function for observable behavior; (5) nothing. Then four rules: no tests that scan source text or grep docs/workflows for strings that code can expose directly; no hand-maintained lists of strings that mirror code (error codes, command names, env names) — derive from the type; prefer a crate already in Cargo.lock (semver for versions, miette/thiserror for errors, clap derive for args, serde for formats, insta for snapshots) over a hand-written grammar; every new error code, JSON key or flag is permanent after 1.0, so prefer fewer broader ones. One line on deletion: before adding a check, delete one that a type now covers. Do not edit anything else.\n\nREPORT (under 80 words): the diff size, commit signed?, doc-check and pre-push exit results.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/aca1afeff7f8ec7a9.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0b1d8b4a-b6ec-4bd1-937c-fdcbe60c841b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error