{"parentUuid":"4b3c9bc8-9996-4563-9cf3-e06b445e021b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"49b8f5ac-1c5c-419a-8735-f668f173dabf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LNweoHUUet5KFfK3vSfV2t","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a3264fad8587e83c7 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a3264fad8587e83c7', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a3264fad8587e83c7.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"8092da3e-8dd3-416d-b223-e8216f0262ae","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:19:16.206Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a3264fad8587e83c7","description":"Fix subdir diff and pre tag bugs","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). First: read AGENTS.md. Then `git fetch origin` and `git switch -c fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags origin/main`.\n\nHOUSE RULES (all mandatory)\n- Prefer types and the compiler over tests; delete before adding; no speculative generality; Windows is unsupported; every new error code/JSON key/flag is permanent, so add none.\n- Comments: one short line, only for a non-obvious WHY. Never hard-wrap prose.\n- Commit signed (`git commit -S`). If gpg fails inside the sandbox, retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true. Never use gpgsign=false. No Claude-Session trailers, no claude.ai links in commits.\n- Verify by EXIT CODE, never by reading output: run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (it runs just pre-push, lint, doc-check, test, workflow-contracts and prints PASS/FAIL per step). Commit before running it (a lint step uses git ls-files). All five must PASS.\n- Run each fix's targeted test (red before, green after) before the full verify.\n- Push the branch (`git push -u origin fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags`). Do NOT open a PR. Do NOT write a changeset (the caller does).\n\nTASK: two confirmed bugs.\n1. `crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs` (~lines 62-68): `changed_source_files_since_last_tag` builds object specs `format!(\"{commit}:{directory}\")` and `HEAD:{directory}` for `GitAccess::object_ids`. git resolves `rev:path` from the repo TOP LEVEL, not the cwd. When the callisto workspace is a subdirectory of the git repo (repo/ws), `HEAD:pkg-a` resolves to nothing at both revs, both ids are None, they compare equal, and a package with committed changes since its tag reports `changedSinceLastTag: false`. Fix: use `rev:./dir` and `rev:./` for the workspace root (the empty-directory case currently hashes the whole repo tree). `read_at` in crates/callisto-model/src/vcs/access.rs already uses `rev:./path`; follow it. Regression test with REAL git (look at the real-git helpers in existing tests): git repo at r1/, workspace at r1/ws/ with a cargo package ws/pkg-a, tag pkg-a@0.1.0, then commit a change under ws/pkg-a/src; assert changed_since_last_tag is true. It must fail on current main first.\n2. `validate_tag(tag, dotted)` in `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs` hand-writes SemVer prerelease identifier rules for the dotted case (used by `pre enter`). It accepts `01` and `beta.01`, which are invalid SemVer, so `callisto version` later fails with E035. Replace the dotted check with `semver::Prerelease::new` (the `semver` crate is already a workspace dependency; add it to callisto-graph's Cargo.toml via `semver.workspace = true` only if it is not already a dependency there). Keep the error as the existing `GraphError::TagInvalid` (E324, exit 2). `beta.1`, `rc.2`, `alpha` must still be accepted; `01`, `beta.01`, empty, `a..b`, `a b` rejected. The non-dotted (snapshot) branch is a different grammar and stays. Test the accept/reject table in the existing test module style (rstest is available if the file already uses it).\n\nREPORT (under 150 words): branch, commit SHAs and whether signed, red-before/green-after proof for each bug, the five verify results, anything unproven.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a3264fad8587e83c7.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0b1d8b4a-b6ec-4bd1-937c-fdcbe60c841b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4b3c9bc8-9996-4563-9cf3-e06b445e021b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
