short line, only for a non-obvious WHY. Never hard-wrap prose.\n- Commit signed (`git commit -S`). If gpg fails inside the sandbox, retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true. Never gpgsign=false. No Claude-Session trailers, no claude.ai links.\n- Verify by EXIT CODE: after committing, run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (prints PASS/FAIL per step). All five must PASS.\n- Push (`git push -u origin refactor/note-without-global`). Do NOT open a PR or write a changeset.\n\nTASK: `crates/callisto-graph/src/note.rs` has `note_once` backed by `static SEEN: OnceLock<Mutex<BTreeSet<String>>>`, a process-global used from 8 call sites to print a stderr note only once even when the workspace is loaded more than once. Process-global mutable state is un-Rusty and makes tests order-dependent. First find WHY the same note is emitted twice (which flow loads/resolves the workspace twice, or which loop repeats). Then remove the global with the smallest change: preferably emit the note at the one place that runs once per command (dedupe at the source), or carry a small value (e.g. notes collected during load and printed by the caller) through the existing load path. Do not introduce a new global, a new trait or a new parameter on many signatures; if the only fix needs one, stop and report instead. Keep stderr output byte-identical for the user-visible cases (find the tests that assert the note text and keep them passing; add one test only if no test covers the once-only behavior). Delete `note_once` and the static.\n\nREPORT (under 150 words): why it fired twice, what you changed, net lines, commit signed?, five verify results, anything unproven.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a55946410f1490f50.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0b1d8b4a-b6ec-4bd1-937c-fdcbe60c841b","c