: one short line, only for a non-obvious WHY. Never hard-wrap prose.\n- Commit signed (`git commit -S`), one commit per numbered item below. If gpg fails inside the sandbox, retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true. Never gpgsign=false. No Claude-Session trailers, no claude.ai links.\n- Verify by EXIT CODE: after committing, run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (prints PASS/FAIL per step). All five must PASS.\n- Push (`git push -u origin refactor/delete-redundant-checks`). Do NOT open a PR or write a changeset.\n- Do NOT touch: crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs, tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs, tests/error_code_hygiene_tests.rs, tests/error_envelope_tests.rs, crates/callisto-graph/tests/error_registry_architecture.rs, the `DIAGNOSTIC_CODE_SOURCE_FILES` scanner in crates/callisto-model/src/lib.rs, changed.rs, note.rs (other agents own them).\n\nTASK: delete checks the compiler or an existing lint already enforces. For EACH item first confirm the claim in the code, then delete; if a claim is false, skip that item and say why.\n1. crates/callisto-graph/tests/architecture.rs: delete the `map_err` test, `MAP_ERR_IGNORE_ALLOWLIST` and `contains_map_err_ignore` (workspace clippy already has `map_err_ignore = \"deny\"`, Cargo.toml). Delete `release_intent_stale_is_constructed_only_by_fresh_reobservation` and `stale_reason_constructors_are_module_private` plus `STALE_REASON_REAL_CONSTRUCTORS` if then unused, AFTER confirming the four StaleReason constructors in commands/release/mod.rs really have no visibility modifier (privacy is compiler-enforced). KEEP the manifest-parsing tripwire test and its ALLOWLIST.\n2. crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs ~line 513: delete the `include_str!(\"snapshot.rs\")` test `plan_snapshot_source_never_calls_pre_mutation_checks`.\n3. crates/callisto-model/src/lib.rs: delete `test_auto_traits` (and its helper) only; leave the code scanner alone.\n4. crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs ~58-59: `(Dev, _)` and `_` arms have identical bodies; delete the redundant arm.\n5. crates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs: five tests assert `elapsed < N s` (around lines 882-898, 953-967, 989-1003, 1026-1040, 1487). Remove the elapsed bounds, keep every behavioral assertion. Check the nextest config (.config/nextest.toml or similar) has a per-test timeout that terminates a hang; if it does not, say so in the report and do not add one.\n6. `ApplyPermit::granted_unless_dry_run` takes a bool and architecture.rs has a text-scan test `apply_permits_are_never_granted_from_a_literal` (+ `literal_permit_detector_…` self-test) guarding against literal true/false arguments. Assess the type fix: a `DryRun` newtype (private field, constructed only from the parsed flag) as the parameter so a literal cannot compile. If call sites are few (<=10) and the change is a net deletion of lines, do it and delete both tests; otherwise skip and report the call-site count.\nDo not add new tests except where item 6 needs one.\n\nREPORT (under 200 words): per item done/skipped with reason, net lines removed, commits (signed?), five verify results, anything unproven.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/aa2d6dc58131b8f74.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0b1d8b4a-b6ec-4bd1-937c-fdcbe60c841b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5870cc60-74c4-4422-9abf-ecbe15f026bf","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
