{"parentUuid":"57ffcd73-dc9f-4288-8667-fdcbbe387de3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"49b8f5ac-1c5c-419a-8735-f668f173dabf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hni5GzLay2CHJHmufCpyK5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: aee5b559fb0687d8c (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'aee5b559fb0687d8c', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/aee5b559fb0687d8c.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"5af9f945-0369-4805-a56a-12ca415e7614","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:19:16.363Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"aee5b559fb0687d8c","description":"exit_kind replaces code lists","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). First: read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md. Then `git fetch origin` and `git switch -c refactor/exit-kind origin/main`.\n\nHOUSE RULES (all mandatory)\n- Prefer types and the compiler over tests; delete before adding; no speculative generality; Windows is unsupported; every new error code/JSON key/flag is permanent, so add none and change no code number.\n- Comments: one short line, only for a non-obvious WHY. Never hard-wrap prose.\n- Commit signed (`git commit -S`). If gpg fails inside the sandbox, retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true. Never gpgsign=false. No Claude-Session trailers, no claude.ai links.\n- Verify by EXIT CODE, never by reading output: after committing, run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (just pre-push, lint, doc-check, test, workflow-contracts; prints PASS/FAIL per step). All five must PASS.\n- Push (`git push -u origin refactor/exit-kind`). Do NOT open a PR or write a changeset.\n\nTASK: replace the stringly-typed exit-code classification with a type.\nToday `crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs` has `USAGE_CODES` (29 code strings), `USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES` (E316, E317) and `CliError::is_usage_error()` which stringifies `code()` and matches the lists; `main.rs:~35` maps true to exit 2, else 1. `crates/callisto-cli/tests/usage_exit_codes_tests.rs` holds a ~230-code `RUNTIME_CODES` string and a meta-test checking every code in docs/errors.md is in exactly one list; `error_envelope_tests.rs:~17` also reads the lists.\nReplace with: an `ExitKind` enum (Usage, Runtime) and `fn exit_kind(&self) -> ExitKind` on each error enum that owns a usage variant, written as an exhaustive-by-intent match that names ONLY the usage variants and defaults `_ => ExitKind::Runtime` (runtime is the safe default). Variants: 26 are CliError variants (codes E214 E216 E217 E218 E224-E229 E231 E240 E241 E242 E270 E271 E274 E275 E276 E279 E282 E283 E298 E309 E327 E329); three are GraphError variants in crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs (E195 InitInvalidForgeRepository, E196 InitInvalidTargetTriple, E324 TagInvalid); E316 ColonReference and E317 BareReference are ConfigError variants that count as usage only when their `context` starts with `--` (reachable as CliError::Config and CliError::Graph(GraphError::Config)). CliError delegates to GraphError/ConfigError. Find each variant by grepping `code(E###)`. Put ExitKind where both crates can reach it (callisto-graph, since cli depends on it) unless the layering says otherwise. `main.rs` uses `exit_kind()`.\nDelete: USAGE_CODES, USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES, the string-based `is_usage_error`, RUNTIME_CODES, and the classification meta-test (and whatever in error_envelope_tests.rs or error_code_hygiene_tests.rs consumed the lists; keep any check there that is NOT about the lists). KEEP the binary-driven tests in usage_exit_codes_tests.rs that run the real binary and assert exit 2 / exit 1 (observable behavior) and update imports. Exit codes must be byte-identical to today: before deleting, capture the classification of every documented code from the OLD lists (a scratch script, not committed) and prove the new `exit_kind` yields the same for each variant you can construct; at minimum add one small unit test per enum that constructs one usage variant and one runtime variant, plus a ConfigError test for the `--` context rule. Do not touch docs/errors.md numbering. Fix doc comments that referenced the deleted test.\n\nREPORT (under 200 words): branch, commits (signed?), net lines deleted/added, proof of identical classification, five verify results, anything unproven or any usage variant you could not map.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/aee5b559fb0687d8c.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0b1d8b4a-b6ec-4bd1-937c-fdcbe60c841b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"57ffcd73-dc9f-4288-8667-fdcbbe387de3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"5af9f945-0369-4805-a56a-12ca415e7614","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Agent","toolUseID":"toolu_01Hni5GzLay2CHJHmufCpyK5","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Agent\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":62},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b62eb3e7-f5df-4c1b-b0c9-9430b74e1d97","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:19:16.357Z","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"parentUuid":"b62eb3e7-f5df-4c1b-b0c9-9430b74e1d97","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"sandbox_instructions","content":"## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a limit below is not enforced. Commands can reach more than that — credentials and keys elsewhere on this machine, the user's other projects and configuration, sockets that control this machine or other workloads, cloud metadata endpoints — but being reachable does not make them provided; those are the user's, not the task's, unless the user's request calls for them. If the task cannot be finished with what you were given, do what you can and tell the user plainly what is missing instead of finding another way to it; that report is a complete answer.\n\nHow the sandbox is configured in this session:\nFilesystem: {\"read\":{\"denyOnly\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/ide\",\"~/.config/orin-dx\",\"~/.cache/orin-dx\",\"~/Library/Application Support/OrinDX-PR-Bot\",\"~/Library/Caches/OrinDX-PR-Bot\"],\"allowWithinDeny\":[]},\"write\":{\"allowOnly\":[\"/dev/stdout\",\"/dev/stderr\",\"/dev/null\",\"/dev/tty\",\"/dev/dtracehelper\",\"/dev/autofs_nowait\",\"/tmp/claude\",\"/private/tmp/claude\",\"/Users/gabe/.npm/_logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/debug\",\".\",\"$TMPDIR\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.git\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aca1afeff7f8ec7a9\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a55946410f1490f50\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa2d6dc58131b8f74\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-aee5b559fb0687d8c\"],\"denyWithinAllow\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.d\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/local\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/daemon\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/shell-snapshots\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/session-env\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/workflows\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/commands\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/agents\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/routines\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/rules\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/output-styles\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/launch.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/CLAUDE.md\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/daemon.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature-iat.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.stamp.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/backups\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/loop.md\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/cowork_plugins\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/dev-mods\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/mcp-skill-archives\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/mcp-discovery-cache\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/shares\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/todos\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/statsig\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/access-audit\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/remote-settings-helper-consent\",\"... and 200 more (truncated for prompt size)\"]}}\n\n - You should always default to running commands within the sandbox. Do NOT attempt to set `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` unless:\n  - The user *explicitly* asks you to bypass sandbox\n  - A specific command just failed and you see evidence of sandbox restrictions causing the failure. Note that commands can fail for many reasons unrelated to the sandbox (missing files, wrong arguments, network issues, etc.).\n - Evidence of sandbox-caused failures includes:\n  - \"Operation not permitted\" errors for file/network operations\n  - Access denied to specific paths outside allowed directories\n  - Network connection failures to non-whitelisted hosts\n  - Unix socket connection errors\n - When you see evidence of sandbox-caused failure:\n  - If the `<sandbox_violations>` block names a denied host, re-run the command with that host in its `allowed_domains` (auto mode); otherwise retry with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` directly rather than asking in prose first — the retry itself goes through the permission gate (a user prompt, or the auto-mode classifier when auto mode is active)\n  - Briefly explain what sandbox restriction likely caused the failure. Be sure to mention that the user can use the `/sandbox` command to manage restrictions.\n - A sandbox denial on a credential, a file or a host that the task does not involve is the boundary above at work: tell the user rather than retrying with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`.\n - Treat each command you execute with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` individually. Even if you have recently run a command with this setting, you should default to running future commands within the sandbox.\n - Do not suggest adding sensitive paths like ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, ~/.ssh/*, or credential files to the sandbox allowlist.\n - Network egress goes through a filtering proxy. Attempt requests and read the error rather than predicting whether a host is reachable; denied connections are reported in a `<sandbox_violations>` block explaining the reason. In auto mode, list the hosts a command needs beyond that in its `allowed_domains` — a denied host named in the block goes there on the re-run.\n - If a command fails to bind or listen on a local port with \"Operation not permitted\" (EPERM), local port binding is off in this sandbox. Treat it as the sandbox-caused failure described above, and tell the user that `sandbox.network.allowLocalBinding: true` in their settings (it applies without a restart) allows it without leaving the sandbox.\n - Opening an app, file or URL with `open`, or scripting another app with `osascript`, is blocked inside this sandbox (macOS Launch Services and Apple Events are off) and fails with errors such as -10822 (kLSServerCommunicationErr), -54, -600 or \"LSOpenURLsWithRole() failed\". That failure is the sandbox, not a problem with what you built; do not retry it with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`. Tell the user the sandbox blocked it and give them the exact command to run themselves.\n - For temporary files, always use the `$TMPDIR` environment variable. TMPDIR is automatically set to the correct sandbox-writable directory in sandbox mode. Do NOT use `/tmp` directly - use `$TMPDIR` instead.\n - If a clipboard utility such as `pbcopy`, `xclip`, or `wl-copy` fails inside the sandbox and the user wants the text on their clipboard, put the text in a fenced code block in your response and tell them to run `/copy` (it copies from outside the sandbox; when the picker appears they can select just that block), rather than writing a file for them to copy manually."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3daf1a22-fad2-4437-b2d3-c340d451d9b1","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:19:16.375Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a limit below is not enforced. Commands can reach more than that — credentials and keys elsewhere on this machine, the user's other projects and configuration, sockets that control this machine or other workloads, cloud metadata endpoints — but being reachable does not make them provided; those are the user's, not the task's, unless the user's request calls for them. If the task cannot be finished with what you were given, do what you can and tell the user plainly what is missing instead of finding another way to it; that report is a complete answer.\n\nHow the sandbox is configured in this session:\nFilesystem: {\"read\":{\"denyOnly\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/ide\",\"~/.config/orin-dx\",\"~/.cache/orin-dx\",\"~/Library/Application Support/OrinDX-PR-Bot\",\"~/Library/Caches/OrinDX-PR-Bot\"],\"allowWithinDeny\":[]},\"write\":{\"allowOnly\":[\"/dev/stdout\",\"/dev/stderr\",\"/dev/null\",\"/dev/tty\",\"/dev/dtracehelper\",\"/dev/autofs_nowait\",\"/tmp/claude\",\"/private/tmp/claude\",\"/Users/gabe/.npm/_logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/debug\",\".\",\"$TMPDIR\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.git\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264f