{"parentUuid":"0c50e827-c4e3-4c12-ba80-ab8159805ed1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwm2MQ3MedLrpa6wtFUB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Five agents are running in parallel, each on its own branch in an isolated worktree:\n\n| Agent | Branch | Model, effort |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bug fixes (`rev:./dir`, `semver::Prerelease`) | `fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags` | Sonnet, medium |\n| `exit_kind()` replacing the code lists | `refactor/exit-kind` | Opus, high |\n| Deletions (text-scan tests, wall-clock asserts, cascade arm, `DryRun` newtype) | `refactor/delete-redundant-checks` | Sonnet, medium |\n| `note_once` without the global | `refactor/note-without-global` | Sonnet, medium |\n| `AGENTS.md` invariant-ladder section | `docs/invariant-ladder` | Sonnet, low |\n\n- **Why those models:** Opus with high effort for `exit_kind` because it needs the most judgment, and Sonnet for the rest, which are mechanical or small.\n- **Scope:** I split the file ownership so the agents don't conflict. The deletions agent is told not to touch `error.rs`, the error-code tests, `changed.rs` or `note.rs`.\n- **Rules every agent got:** signed commits, no session links, checks judged by exit code, and push without opening a PR. Each is also told to prefer types, delete before adding, and add no error codes.\n- **Wave 2, once these land:** the `changed.rs` unscoped-diff rewrite (after the bug-fix branch merges) and the error-code scanner collapse (after `exit_kind` merges).\n- **My follow-up:** changesets for the two bug fixes via the courier agents, then PR text via `courier:pr`, then a Brain memory for the invariant ladder.\n\nI'll read each report against its branch before opening any PR.\n\nneeds input: none, I'll report as the agents finish."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15258,"cache_read_input_tokens":22