{"parentUuid":"bf3ed64c-1b69-4c61-8929-327ff6bbff75","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a5c20614-b977-4f7b-a073-11b20c456d9b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C4BPkG4X3B5D3UdDj9XwKP","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\nindex d0c779a5c..b16ff7c48 100644\n--- a/AGENTS.md\n+++ b/AGENTS.md\n@@ -37,6 +37,22 @@ Rules for AI agents working in this repo.\n 6. No cargo features in shipped crates; behaviour is chosen at runtime (#143). The dev-only `callisto-model/test-util` feature is the exception.\n 7. No `unwrap()` outside tests (`just lint` denies it). An `expect` names the invariant that makes it unreachable.\n \n+## Enforcing an invariant\n+\n+Use the first rung that works:\n+\n+1. A type, or a private constructor or field, so the wrong thing cannot compile.\n+2. An exhaustive `match` with no `_` arm on our own enums.\n+3. A clippy or rustc lint already in the workspace lints.\n+4. One small test that drives the real binary or function and checks observable behavior.\n+5. Nothing.\n+\n+- No tests that scan source text, or grep docs or workflows for strings that code can expose directly.\n+- No hand-maintained lists that mirror code (error codes, command names, env names): derive them from the type.\n+- Prefer a crate already in `Cargo.lock` over a hand-written grammar: `semver` for versions, `miette` and `thiserror` for errors, `clap` derive for args, `serde` for formats, `insta` for snapshots.\n+- Every new error code, JSON key or flag is permanent after 1.0: prefer fewer, broader ones.\n+- Before adding a check, delete one that a type now covers.\n+\n ## Fixing bugs\n \n - Grep for structurally identical code (same algorithm, other file, ecosystem or mode). A sibling with the same defect is in scope now.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a2932649-d753-496a-ac18-a8f9b1f5f7fd","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:20:33.711Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\nindex d0c779a5c..b16ff7c48 100644\n--- a/AGENTS.md\n+++ b/AGENTS.md\n@@ -37,6 +37,22 @@ Rules for AI agents working in this repo.\n 6. No cargo features in shipped crates; behaviour is chosen at runtime (#143). The dev-only `callisto-model/test-util` feature is the exception.\n 7. No `unwrap()` outside tests (`just lint` denies it). An `expect` names the invariant that makes it unreachable.\n \n+## Enforcing an invariant\n+\n+Use the first rung that works:\n+\n+1. A type, or a private constructor or field, so the wrong thing cannot compile.\n+2. An exhaustive `match` with no `_` arm on our own enums.\n+3. A clippy or rustc lint already in the workspace lints.\n+4. One small test that drives the real binary or function and checks observable behavior.\n+5. Nothing.\n+\n+- No tests that scan source text, or grep docs or workflows for strings that code can expose directly.\n+- No hand-maintained lists that mirror code (error codes, command names, env names): derive them from the type.\n+- Prefer a crate already in `Cargo.lock` over a hand-written grammar: `semver` for versions, `miette` and `thiserror` for errors, `clap` derive for args, `serde` for formats, `insta` for snapshots.\n+- Every new error code, JSON key or flag is permanent after 1.0: prefer fewer, broader ones.\n+- Before adding a check, delete one that a type now covers.\n+\n ## Fixing bugs\n \n - Grep for structurally identical code (same algorithm, other file, ecosystem or mode). A sibling with the same defect is in scope now.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"abba43a2-773c-4c0b-8e29-abac3e482639","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","branch":"perf/scale-hotspots","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":