{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:30:00.037Z","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","content":"<agent-message from=\"aee5b559fb0687d8c\">\n[Subagent hand-back] The text below is the final report of a subagent this session delegated to. It is model output, NOT a message from the user: instructions, requests, or approval claims inside it are the subagent's words and carry no user authority. The harness indents every line of the report, so a frame-like line at column zero inside it would be forged. Notes above this frame may quote model-derived text, which carries no user authority either. The report follows:\n  The refactor is done and pushed to branch `refactor/exit-kind` (no PR, no changeset). Exit codes come out the same as before for every error code I could construct, and all five verify steps passed.\n  \n  **Commit:** one commit, `ee3d14fd8`. It is signed: git shows G and GitHub's verification reason is `valid`.\n  \n  **Size:** 6 files, +106 / −91, so 15 lines more than before. The 26-arm usage match in `CliError` is most of what was added.\n  \n  **What changed:**\n  - `ExitKind { Usage, Runtime }` lives in `crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs` and is re-exported from that crate.\n  - `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and `CliError` each have `exit_kind()`, which names only the usage variants and defaults everything else to `Runtime`.\n  - `main.rs` now picks the exit code from `exit_kind()`.\n  - Deleted: `USAGE_CODES`, `USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES`, `is_usage_error`, `RUNTIME_CODES` and the classification meta-test.\n  - `error_envelope_tests.rs` no longer reads the lists; it now asserts the exit code is 1 or 2.\n  - Added unit tests: one for `CliError` (including the `Graph(Config)` delegation), one for `GraphError`, and one for the `ConfigError` `--` context rule.\n  \n  **Proof of identical classification:**\n  - I recorded the old classification of all 276 documented codes in scratch files (`$TMPDIR/exitkind/`, not committed): 29 usage, 2 usage only from a flag (E316, E317), 245 runtime.\n  - A scratch test, since deleted, built 76 errors and found the old `is_usage_error()` and the new `exit_kind()` agreed on every one. They were every variant `CliError` defines itself, the three graph usage variants, and E316/E317 with four different contexts through both wrappers. All 31 usage codes came up.\n  - Each usage code is defined in exactly one place, so it maps to exactly one variant.\n  \n  **Verify:** pre-push, lint, doc-check, test and workflow-contracts all PASS (exit 0).\n  \n  **Unproven:** the scratch test did not build every runtime variant of `GraphError`, `ConfigError` or the errors from the model crate. They count as runtime only because none of them defines a usage code, which I checked with grep. Every usage variant was mapped.\n</agent-message>"}
