{"parentUuid":"5ca4e08f-aea4-4fdc-acf1-725fbf4dc551","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e493b078-92a2-46dc-b961-6c0ca8e3901f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:31:05.623Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3658a1f85bca2d75","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"perf/scale-hotspots","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"beb80b34310792598932f6db1858f46f2a36cacbf78ed9b4e81891fe038e1373","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The repo has a PR template, so I'm putting all three bodies in its format and keeping the agents' content."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CXNRVqvYYpNVMZDvhqiG7e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_exitkind.md","content":"## Summary\n- Exit-code classification was stringly typed: `USAGE_CODES`, `USAGE_WHEN_FROM_FLAG_CODES`, a string-matching `is_usage_error`, and a ~230-code `RUNTIME_CODES` string kept honest by a meta-test. This replaces all of it with `ExitKind { Usage, Runtime }` and an `exit_kind()` method on `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and `CliError`. Each names only its usage variants and defaults to `Runtime`, and `main.rs` maps `Usage` to exit 2.\n- Exit codes are unchanged. A scratch test (not committed) compared the old `is_usage_error` with the new `exit_kind` on 76 error values built from every usage variant, covering all 31 usage codes including E316 and E317 (`--` flags vs `callisto.toml`). The runtime variants of `GraphError`, `ConfigError` and the model errors were not all built; they count as runtime because none defines a usage code.\n- Tradeoff: a new usage error must be added to its `exit_kind` match deliberately. Before, the meta-test failed when a documented code was unclassified; now an unlisted variant exits 1. Net +15 lines (+106/-91).\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor: no CLI flag, output or `callisto.toml` change.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: no observable behavior change.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n- [ ] Not run: CI, and `just ci` as a single target\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VW3VdZiNLZJubeomyQg7N1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_delete.md","content":"## Summary\n- Deletes 143 lines of tests and code that duplicate what the compiler already enforces, so they can no longer fail or drift independently of it.\n- Removed: two source-scanning tests for the `StaleReason` constructors (they have no visibility modifier, so privacy is compiler-enforced); the `snapshot.rs` `include_str!` test that grepped its own source; `test_auto_traits` in `callisto-model`; a redundant `(Dev, _)` match arm in `cascade.rs`; five wall-clock `elapsed < N s` assertions in `runner.rs` tests. All behavioral assertions in those runner tests stay, and a hang is still killed by nextest's slow-timeout (120s x4).\n- Deliberately kept: the `map_err` source-scan test, because clippy's `map_err_ignore` only flags bare `|_|` while the test also catches `|_ident|` (five allowlisted files still use it). The apply-permit literal scan also stays, because a `DryRun` newtype would be a net addition (`.dry_run` is read in 41 places).\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Internal refactor: tests and internal code only, no CLI, output or `callisto.toml` change.\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: tests and internal code only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] None apply: no flow, flag, config key or spec'd behavior changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check`, `just test` and `just workflow-contracts` exit 0\n- [ ] Not run: CI, and `just ci` as a single target\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D3n8BQRyea1cPfFPjtdapU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/pr_docs.md","content":"## Summary\n- Adds an \"Enforcing an invariant\" section to AGENTS.md. It tells agents to pick the first rung that works: a type or private constructor, an exhaustive `match` on our own enums, a lint already in the workspace, one small test that drives the real binary or function, or nothing.\n- It also rules out tests that scan source text, hand-maintained lists that mirror code, hand-written grammars when a crate in `Cargo.lock` already does the job, and freely adding error codes, JSON keys or flags (permanent after 1.0).\n- Why: the 0.20 stability batch shipped shell scripts plus text files, a source-text scan, a 21-invocation test that duplicated a trait guarantee, and a 230-string code list. Agents were never told to prefer types, so they reached for text checks.\n\n## Type of change\n- [x] Documentation only\n\n## Changeset\n- [x] None needed: contributor docs only.\n\n## Docs\n- [x] AGENTS.md is the only file changed; no spec, `docs/config.md` or `docs/errors.md` change applies.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] `just doc-check` and `just pre-push` exit 0\n- [ ] Not run: CI\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
