{"parentUuid":"99539fed-4d84-4ea0-a68e-094a58084678","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwpJSmnc44zXKEmBVpBT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013oGBqMtp93yrFVFH9KsjV4","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Duplicate workspace load investigation","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"READ-ONLY investigation; do not edit, commit or push. Repo: orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI), checkout /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7 (branch fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags, = origin/main plus a small fix). Read AGENTS.md first. Principles: prefer types and the compiler, delete before adding, no speculative generality.\n\nQuestion: the same workspace is loaded more than once in a single command, which (a) costs time on large repos and (b) is why `note_once` (crates/callisto-graph/src/note.rs, a process-global `static SEEN: OnceLock<Mutex<BTreeSet<String>>>`, 8 call sites) exists. Known sites: `init` loads in `detect` then `preview` (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/init.rs); the release flows load once in `load_workspace` and `validate_release_intent` loads again via `Workspace::load` in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/capability.rs. Find EVERY command path that calls `Workspace::load` (or equivalent locator walk, `ProjectLocator::projects_and_platform_candidates`) more than once per invocation.\nFor each duplicate: (1) is the second load needed (does state change between the loads, e.g. a file written, so a fresh read is the point) or redundant; (2) the smallest change that removes it by passing the already-loaded `&Workspace` (not new globals, not a new trait, avoid signature churn across many callers; if a signature must change, count callers); (3) measure: time a command on a large synthetic workspace if the repo has a fixture generator (see callisto-fixtures, benches in crates/callisto-cli/benches, or the 1,800-package setup described in the perf PR #507), or count `walk` invocations with a quick debug counter in a scratch copy outside the repo (do not modify the checkout); report the cost of the second load. (4) Would removing all redundant loads make `note_once` unnecessary? List which of its 8 call sites would still fire twice.\nReport under 400 words: a table (command path, file:line of both loads, needed or redundant, fix size, measured cost), then a recommendation ranked by value. If nothing is worth changing, say so plainly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2191,"cache_read_input_tokens":313668,"output_tokens":2825,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":905},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2191,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2825,"cache_read_input_tokens":313668,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2191},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013oGBqMtp93yrFVFH9KsjV4":{"description":"Duplicate workspace load investigation","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"medium","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"READ-ONLY investigation; do not edit, commit or push. Repo: orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI), checkout /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7 (branch fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags, = origin/main plus a small fix). Read AGENTS.md first. Principles: prefer types and the compiler, delete before adding, no speculative generality.\n\nQuestion: the same workspace is loaded more than once in a single command, which (a) costs time on large repos and (b) is why `note_once` (crates/callisto-graph/src/note.rs, a process-global `static SEEN: OnceLock<Mutex<BTreeSet<String>>>`, 8 call sites) exists. Known sites: `init` loads in `detect` then `preview` (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/init.rs); the release flows load once in `load_workspace` and `validate_release_intent` loads again via `Workspace::load` in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/capability.rs. Find EVERY command path that calls `Workspace::load` (or equivalent locator walk, `ProjectLocator::projects_and_platform_candidates`) more than once per invocation.\nFor each duplicate: (1) is the second load needed (does state change between the loads, e.g. a file written, so a fresh read is the point) or redundant; (2) the smallest change that removes it by passing the already-loaded `&Workspace` (not new globals, not a new trait, avoid signature churn across many callers; if a signature must change, count callers); (3) measure: time a command on a large synthetic workspace if the repo has a fixture generator (see callisto-fixtures, benches in crates/callisto-cli/benches, or the 1,800-package setup described in the perf PR #507), or count `walk` invocations with a quick debug counter in a scratch copy outside the repo (do not modify the checkout); report the cost of the second load. (4) Would removing all redundant loads make `note_once` unnecessary? List which of its 8 call sites would still fire twice.\nReport under 400 words: a table (command path, file:line of both loads, needed or redundant, fix size, measured cost), then a recommendation ranked by value. If nothing is worth changing, say so plainly."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a9225c90-5e7c-4d09-b0c4-1942aeaec683","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwpJSVvahiDgke78EKtG","requestRef":"ff066901-b810-4448-99ce-9f66a71ff06b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"81d35c54-debe-42f8-8e68-29d5d64ea90b",