the same workspace is loaded more than once in a single command, which (a) costs time on large repos and (b) is why `note_once` (crates/callisto-graph/src/note.rs, a process-global `static SEEN: OnceLock<Mutex<BTreeSet<String>>>`, 8 call sites) exists. Known sites: `init` loads in `detect` then `preview` (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/init.rs); the release flows load once in `load_workspace` and `validate_release_intent` loads again via `Workspace::load` in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/release/capability.rs. Find EVERY command path that calls `Workspace::load` (or equivalent locator walk, `ProjectLocator::projects_and_platform_candidates`) more than once per invocation.\nFor each duplicate: (1) is the second load needed (does state change between the loads, e.g. a file written, so a fresh read is the point) or redundant; (2) the smallest change that removes it by passing the already-loaded `&Workspace` (not new globals, not a new trait, avoid signature churn across many callers; if a signature must change, count callers); (3) measure: time a command on a large synthetic workspace if the repo has a fixture generator (see callisto-fixtures, benches in crates/callisto-cli/benches, or the 1,800-package setup described in the perf PR #507), or count `walk` invocations with a quick debug counter in a scratch copy outside the repo (do not modify the checkout); report the cost of the second load. (4) Would removing all redundant loads make `note_once` unnecessary? List which of its 8 call sites would still fire twice.\nReport under 400 words: a table (command path, file:line of both loads, needed or redundant, fix size, measured cost), then a recommendation ranked by value. If nothing is worth changing, say so plainly.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/a85dbd6870bf15492.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a9225c90-5e7c-4d09-b0c4-