{"parentUuid":"9f5193ef-1996-4c01-8e70-d0d7c412e83b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwpnqSLRPUe42MmBz81C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GW3EHQabEYsA17gVH9DHhF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Align CLI spec and help with 1.0 contract","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","effort":"low","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You work in an isolated git worktree of orin-dx/callisto (Rust release CLI). First: read AGENTS.md and docs/stability.md. Then `git fetch origin` and `git switch -c docs/align-cli-spec-with-exit-codes origin/main`.\n\nHOUSE RULES: commit signed (`git commit -S`; if gpg fails inside the sandbox retry that same command with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links; never hard-wrap prose; terse comments. Verify by EXIT CODE: after committing run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (prints PASS/FAIL for pre-push, lint, doc-check, test, workflow-contracts); all five must PASS. Push (`git push -u origin docs/align-cli-spec-with-exit-codes`). Do NOT open a PR; no changeset. Add no error code, flag or key.\n\nTASK: three confirmed doc/code mismatches; docs are wrong, code is right (docs/stability.md: exit 2 = bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing; the code's classification is `USAGE_CODES` in crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs, or `exit_kind` if it exists on your base).\n1. docs/specs/cli.json states exit code 1 for failures the binary exits 2 on. Update the criteria text only, keeping ids: CLI-OUT-06 and CLI-OUT-07 (generic failure: exit 1, but a usage error exits 2, link to docs/stability.md wording), CLI-ADD-04 (E214), CLI-ADD-05 (missing/empty --summary, E274), CLI-ADD-06 (missing `:severity` or unknown severity exit 2, E270; an unknown package name is E102 and stays exit 1 — read the criterion and keep each clause accurate), CLI-INIT-10 (E240/E241), CLI-INIT-11 (E242), CLI-INIT-12 (E195/E196), CLI-SURF-06 (unknown command, E283). For EACH criterion, verify by running the binary (`cargo run -q -p callisto-cli -- ...` in a temp fixture dir under $TMPDIR) that the stated exit code is what actually happens before editing; do not change a criterion whose stated code is already right. Also CLI-OUT-06 lists the JSON error envelope as {schemaVersion, command, error}: add `dryRun` if the code emits it (crates/callisto-cli/src/error.rs format_error_json).\n2. `snapshot --tag` help (crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs ~248: \"e.g. a commit SHA or branch name\") is wrong: only letters, digits and `-` are accepted, so `feature/x` fails E324. Reword the doc comment to say that in one short line (for example \"letters, digits and `-` only, e.g. a short commit SHA or PR number\"). Update any snapshot of the help text (crates/callisto-cli/tests/cmd/*.trycmd, insta snapshots) and docs/specs/cli.json CLI-SNAP-01 if it repeats the claim.\n3. Do NOT touch docs/config.md pre-major-inference (owner decision pending) or docs/errors.md wording.\n\nREPORT (under 120 words): which criteria you changed (and any you left because they were already right), the help change, commit signed?, five verify results."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":848,"cache_read_input_tokens":326622,"output_tokens":2546,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":848,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2546,"cache_read_input_tokens":326622,"cache_creation_input_tokens":848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_