{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","hash":"5cf831fa22db86084b9c2f028067c93c527a53aeee9120bf35c687c7cd7abb23","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Dc4bq2LQ9KDH8dG9iX3Jm","type":"tool_result","content":"(Bash completed with no output)","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014iQUi6LahQow5QatqQYXJQ","type":"tool_result","content":" crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs |  2 +-\n docs/specs/cli.json            | 18 +++++++++---------\n 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)\n-    /// Tag to append to the snapshot version (e.g. a commit SHA or branch name).\n+    /// Tag to append to the snapshot version (letters, digits and `-` only, e.g. a short commit SHA or PR number).\n-      \"criterion\": \"`callisto help` prints the root help; `callisto help <command>` (nested names accepted as multiple words) prints that subcommand's help; an unknown command name exits 1 naming it. `callisto completions <shell>` never offers a hidden subcom\n+      \"criterion\": \"`callisto help` prints the root help; `callisto help <command>` (nested names accepted as multiple words) prints that subcommand's help; an unknown command name exits 2 with `E283` naming it. `callisto completions <shell>` never offers a h\n-      \"criterion\": \"When a command fails under `--format json`, stderr ends with a JSON object `{\\\"schemaVersion\\\", \\\"command\\\", \\\"error\\\": {\\\"code\\\", \\\"message\\\", \\\"help\\\", \\\"path\\\"}}` and the exit code is 1; `command` is the subcommand that was parsed and `\n+      \"criterion\": \"When a command fails under `--format json`, stderr ends with a JSON object `{\\\"schemaVersion\\\", \\\"command\\\", \\\"dryRun\\\", \\\"error\\\": {\\\"code\\\", \\\"message\\\", \\\"help\\\", \\\"path\\\"}}` and the exit code is 1, or 2 for a usage error as defined in \n-      \"criterion\": \"When a command fails under text format, stderr shows a diagnostic with an error code and a message, and the exit code is 1.\",\n+      \"criterion\": \"When a command fails under text format, stderr shows a diagnostic with an error code and a message, and the exit code is 1, or 2 for a usage error as defined in docs/stability.md.\",\n-      \"criterion\": \"`callisto add` with no --package and a non-terminal stdin exits 1 with error `E214` whose help names `callisto add --package <name>:<severity>`.\",\n+      \"criterion\": \"`callisto add` with no --package and a non-terminal stdin exits 2 with error `E214` whose help names `callisto add --package <name>:<severity>`.\",\n-      \"criterion\": \"`add --package` without --summary, or with a whitespace-only summary, exits 1 naming --summary and writes nothing.\",\n+      \"criterion\": \"`add --package` without --summary, or with a whitespace-only summary, exits 2 naming --summary (`E274` when missing, `E275` when empty) and writes nothing.\",\n-      \"criterion\": \"A --package value missing `:severity`, with an unknown severity, or naming a package not in the workspace exits 1 and writes nothing; an unknown package name reports E102, a name without its ecosystem reports E317, and the colon form repor\n+      \"criterion\": \"A --package value missing `:severity`, with an unknown severity, or naming a package not in the workspace writes nothing; a missing `:severity` exits 2 with `E270`, an unknown severity exits 2 with `E271`, an unknown package name exits 1 w\n-      \"criterion\": \"With a non-terminal stdin and no --yes, init exits 1 with `E240` naming --yes and every other missing flag; with --yes it exits 1 with `E241` naming each missing flag: --forge-repository when --artifact-target is given, and --product-packa\n+      \"criterion\": \"With a non-terminal stdin and no --yes, init exits 2 with `E240` naming --yes and every other missing flag; with --yes it exits 2 with `E241` naming each missing flag: --forge-repository when --artifact-target is given, and --product-packa\n-      \"criterion\": \"With --yes, omitting --artifact-target writes no `[release]` table; --artifact-target is repeatable and comma-separated, and --workflow with --no-workflow exits 1 with `E242` before writing.\",\n+      \"criterion\": \"With --yes, omitting --artifact-target writes no `[release]` table; --artifact-target is repeatable and comma-separated, and --workflow with --no-workflow exits 2 with `E242` before writing.\",\n-      \"criterion\": \"init exits 1 without writing for an empty or repeated target triple, --artifact-target when no supported Cargo package produces a binary, a --product-package that is absent or not a supported Cargo binary producer, a --forge-repository tha\n+      \"criterion\": \"init exits without writing: 2 for an empty or repeated target triple (`E196`), a --forge-repository that is not `owner/repo` (`E195`), or --forge-repository or --product-package given without --artifact-target (`E298`); 1 for --artifact-ta","is_error":false},{"type":"text","text":"The user sent a new message while you were working:\nMerged all of the previous PRs, what's next?\n\nThis is how Claude Code surfaces messages the user sends mid-turn — within the running turn, often alongside the next tool result, rather than as a separate conversation turn. Address the message above as you continue this turn."}]}}
