{"parentUuid":"642a3e8d-7fcf-49a8-809e-fbe3cf9f287c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwqkgsTaK7q3spU19Hvh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MCC9omJe9rYgSUAC1bHXLA","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"PR text for changed.rs rewrite","subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","effort":"low","prompt":"Write a PR title and body for orin-dx/callisto branch `refactor/changed-files-without-pathspecs` (base main), using the repo template .github/pull_request_template.md sections (Summary, Type of change, Changeset, Docs, Test Plan). Diff: `git diff origin/main...origin/refactor/changed-files-without-pathspecs` (run from /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7; do not cd elsewhere). Facts: `changed_source_files_since_last_tag` in crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs already ran one git diff per distinct tag commit; what remained was pathspec scoping plus chunking (`PATHSPEC_BUDGET = 24_000`, `list_in_chunks`, `exclude_pathspec`, a `budget` parameter) that existed for a Windows command-line limit, and Windows is unsupported. Now: each distinct tag commit runs one unscoped `GitAccess::paths_differing_from(commit)` (the existing `--no-renames --relative --name-only -z` diff), all untagged packages share one `ls-files` through a new 4-line `GitAccess::tracked_paths()`, paths are filtered by a `globset` matcher built with `literal_separator(true)` (a trailing `/` pattern becomes `**/dir/**`, anything else `**/pat`, as before) and mapped to packages with the existing `SpecIndex`. Net +63/-138 across changed.rs and vcs/access.rs. Output is unchanged for the default ignore list; the only production caller passes `DEFAULT_IGNORED_PATHS`. Differences from git's pathspec magic: globset treats `{a,b}` as alternation (git does not) but no default pattern uses braces and users cannot supply ignore patterns; a package with no manifests used to match every file and now matches none (discovery never produces one); an invalid ignore pattern panics via `expect` naming the invariant, because no error code was added. One improvement: a package directory with glob characters like `pkg[1]` is now matched literally, with a new real-git test (a `pkg[1]` package next to a `pkg1` sibling). Verify: just pre-push, lint, doc-check, test, workflow-contracts exit 0; CI has not run. Not measured: the diff on a very large workspace. No changeset: no user-visible change except the `pkg[1]` edge case. Rules: succinct, plain, one line per paragraph (never hard-wrap), no emoji, no AI slop, no session links or Claude trailers. Return JSON per your contract."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":717,"cache_read_input_tokens":377354,"output_tokens":1174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":717,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":377354,"cache_creation_input_tokens":717,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":717},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MCC9omJe9rYgSUAC1bHXLA":{"description":"PR text for changed.rs rewrite","subagent_type":"courier:pr-narrator","model":"sonnet","effort":"low","prompt":"Write a PR title and body for orin-dx/callisto branch `refactor/changed-files-without-pathspecs` (base main), using the repo template .github/pull_request_template.md sections (Summary, Type of change, Changeset, Docs, Test Plan). Diff: `git diff origin/main...origin/refactor/changed-files-without-pathspecs` (run from /