{"parentUuid":"454da981-d4da-444a-a0b6-41c0e8974fd0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwqmKWrNdmaci6xkcuSv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#513 (the scanner collapse) is open, and the `changed.rs` rewrite passes my review, with its PR text being written.\n\n- **Rewrite:** +63/−138 across `changed.rs` and `vcs/access.rs`. It deletes `PATHSPEC_BUDGET`, `list_in_chunks`, `exclude_pathspec` and the Windows-only chunking. It runs one unscoped diff per tag commit and filters through `globset`.\n- **Checks and signature:** all five repo checks exit 0, per the agent, and GitHub reports the commit `valid`.\n- **Output:** unchanged for the default ignore list. The only production caller passes `DEFAULT_IGNORED_PATHS`.\n- **One difference:** `{a,b}` is treated as alternation by `globset` and not by git. No default pattern uses braces and users can't supply ignore patterns, so nothing reaches it today.\n- **Improvement:** a `pkg[1]` directory is now matched literally, with a new real-git test.\n- **Not measured:** the diff on a very large workspace. The cost should be small, since the unscoped diff lists only files changed since the tag, but that's unverified.\n\nI'll open the PR when the text returns. PR #512 (CLI spec exit codes) and #513 are open for your review, along with the pending decisions on exit-2 consistency and the `pre-major-inference` alias.\n\nneeds input: the two pending decisions, whenever you're ready."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1641,"cache_read_input_tokens":378071,"output_tokens":486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1641,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_to