ckage next to a `pkg1` sibling confirms the glob characters are matched literally.\\n- [ ] Not measured: the diff on a very large workspace. Each tag commit still runs one diff as before, so no change is expected (inferred).\\n\\n## Risk and follow-up\\n\\nBehavior differences from git's pathspec magic, none reachable today:\\n- `globset` treats `{a,b}` as alternation and git does not. No default pattern uses braces and users cannot supply ignore patterns.\\n- A package with no manifests used to match every file and now matches none. Discovery never produces such a package.\\n- An invalid ignore pattern panics via `expect`, with a message naming the invariant. No error code was added, since the patterns are static defaults.\"}"},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":217,"turnIndex":296},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3264fad8587e83c7","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/subdir-diff-and-pre-tags","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
