{"parentUuid":"857cc307-8bf5-477d-b103-bd4f1b087dc7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwqoMrYF3LC3fCfUiDDY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #514 (the `changed.rs` rewrite) is open, so wave 2 is complete. The three open PRs from this wave:\n\n| PR | Content |\n|---|---|\n| #512 | Aligns `docs/specs/cli.json` with the exit codes the binary returns, and fixes the `snapshot --tag` help. |\n| #513 | One registry test replaces the overlapping error-code scanners (net −244 lines). |\n| #514 | Removes the pathspec chunking in `changed.rs`; the output is unchanged. |\n\nAll three have signed commits (GitHub shows `valid` for #513 and #514) and their five checks exit 0 locally. CI hasn't run on any of them. The three don't overlap in files.\n\n**Still waiting on you**\n1. Should bad flag values uniformly exit 2? Unknown `--package` exits 1 (E102) while E227 exits 2.\n2. Should `pre-major-inference = \"false\"` be documented as an alias or removed?\n\n**After these merge:**\n- Refresh release PR #493 (0.20.0), which is blocked, and read its changelog.\n- Write the Brain memory for the invariant ladder.\n- Delete the leftover local `worktree-agent-*` branches, once you say your review is done.\n\nneeds input: the two decisions, plus a go on the #493 refresh after the merges."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_read_input_tokens":383355,"output_tokens":442,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":231,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":383355,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_toke