{"parentUuid":"a412f501-b82b-4081-89f3-d4b793ad323b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwud48sAhCe16Vkuf9dV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't verify or fix the finding, because the code it describes isn't in the local Caliper checkout.\n\n- **Repo:** `crates/semantic/src/convert.rs` and `component.rs` exist only in `~/Projects/caliper` (and a homebrew-tap copy). They aren't in Callisto.\n- **Why not checked:** the local Caliper `main` (at `43b512ad`) has `convert.rs` at 240 lines and `component.rs` at 150, and `states_bases` appears nowhere in it. The finding cites lines 399–402 and 188–189, so change #224 must be a Caliper branch or PR I don't have checked out.\n- **What I can't do here:** this session's write access is limited to Callisto worktrees, so I can't edit Caliper even with the right branch.\n\n**What the finding claims:** for a component taking `Props<string>` where `interface Props<T> extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement> { value: T }`, the instantiated interface has only reference flags, so `states_bases` rejects it. The traversal stops and the empty base list replaces the structural composition, so `HTMLAttributes` is dropped from the output. The proposed fix is to follow the generic target during the name-only traversal so the React bases are kept.\n\n**Whether to apply it:** the described fix is plausible, since the failure comes from an instantiated generic losing its target's bases. Before changing anything I'd want a regression test with that exact `Props<string>` shape.\n\nneeds input: the Caliper branch or PR for change #224, and a session working in the Caliper repo. I can start one there, or you can paste the branch name and I'll read it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":280,"cache_read_input_tokens":401706,"output_tokens":546,"output_tokens_d