{"parentUuid":"36605f52-11f3-448e-b1b8-724417fe9316","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwxFAZ4orbVmTZvZG6sZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #516 is Dependabot's bump of `taiki-e/install-action` (2.88.0 to 2.90.1). It fails two checks for unrelated reasons, and Entire Gates also failed after 10 minutes (I didn't look into that one, and it may just follow the others).\n\n**1. Workflow Contracts (caused by the PR)**\n- Dependabot updated the pin in four workflow files (`callisto-ci.yml`, `callisto-advisories.yml`, `callisto-quality.yml`, `callisto-release.yml`) but not in the composite action `.github/actions/install-workflow-linters/action.yml`.\n- That left the repo pinned to two commits (`86f7a0f…` and `c509219…`), and `verify-action-pins.sh` fails on that.\n- Fix: bump that one `uses:` line to the new pin (`c509219cf42fba86913069efd0ade2458c59337b`, v2.90.1) on the Dependabot branch. Dependabot probably skips `.github/actions/**` because its config doesn't list that directory, so this will recur on every bump.\n\n**2. Test Suite (macos-latest) (not caused by the PR)**\n- One test failed out of 2,120 run: `callisto-manifests python::tests::requirement_parse_render_parse_is_idempotent`, a proptest that found a random failing input.\n- The input was `¡[\\u{b}[` (an invalid-looking Python requirement). The first parse gives extras `[]`, but re-parsing the rendered form gives extras `[\"[\"]`.\n- It's a real latent bug in Python requirement parse/render idempotency, found by chance rather than by this change. A re-run would probably pass, since the input is random.\n- Proptest suggested adding its seed (`cc 2c578f3e…`) to `crates/callisto-manifests/proptest-regressions/python/tests.txt` so it fails reliably.\n\n**Proposed next steps**\n- Push the one-line pin fix to the Dependabot branch, or add `/.github/actions/` to the Dependabot config so future bumps cover it.\n- Fix the Python requirement bug in its own PR, adding the regression seed. This needs a look at how the parser treats a stray `[` inside extras.\n- Re-run the checks.\n\nneeds input: say go and I'll push the pin fix to the Dependabot branch (so #516 can merge) and start the Python parser fix as a separate PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":866,"cache_read_input_tokens":429358,"output_tokens":1013,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":210},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1013,"cache_read_input_tokens":429358,"cache_creation_input_tokens":866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":866},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"39b1c44e-13c8-48f2-b3f6-e297c59dbf58","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwxFAHh1ZhCbk5cXWQsg","requestRef":"6078cfa9-ae1c-4ca6-9656-e90ea715d237","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3159cb85-8892-4862-9de5-d34876705e2c","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:46:33.335Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/drop-false-inference-alias","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
