rser should reject/normalise a stray `[` or whitespace-in-extras (vertical tab is whitespace for some checks and not others, `char::is_whitespace` vs ASCII), or the renderer should not emit something the parser reads differently. Prefer a fix where the parser and renderer share one definition (e.g. one whitespace/extras rule) over patching a symptom. Do not change behavior for valid PEP 508 requirements; run the existing python tests. Add the proptest regression line to crates/callisto-manifests/proptest-regressions/python/tests.txt (create if needed, same format as other regression files in the repo). Then run the proptest with a high case count once (e.g. PROPTEST_CASES=20000 cargo nextest run -p callisto-manifests requirement_parse_render) to look for sibling failures; if it finds more, fix the same root cause or report them.\nREPORT (under 200 words): root cause, the fix, red/green proof, whether the high-case run found more, commit signed?, five verify results."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49,"cache_read_input_tokens":432317,"output_tokens":8580,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2322},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8580,"cache_read_input_tokens":432317,"cache_creation_input_tokens":49,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":49},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016PnicRHk3jcWYeJZY4xk7t":{"description":"Fix Python requirement idempotency","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","effort":"medium","isolation":"worktree","run_in_background