orted, new public surface is permanent at 1.0.\nEarlier audits covered: stringly-typed exit/error-code lists (done), source-text scan tests (done), wall-clock asserts (done), Windows pathspec chunking (done), credential-name lists (no leak, left), global note_once (kept). NOT yet checked, evaluate each with counts and evidence:\n1. Near-identical tests that `rstest` (already a dev-dependency, 5 uses today) or a table could collapse: find the 10 largest clusters of copy-pasted test bodies differing only in inputs (crates/*/src/**/tests*, crates/*/tests). Report cluster, instance count, lines that a table would save.\n2. Flag soup: `bool` parameters or several `bool` fields that can contradict (should be an enum), `Option` fields only valid together, in non-test code. e.g. the four `has_*` bools in crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/init.rs ~90-100, command arg structs, report structs. Report the worst 8 with file:line and what type would make the bad state unrepresentable.\n3. Hand-rolled functionality where a crate already in Cargo.lock/Cargo.toml fits: crates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs (subprocess runner with a 50 ms try_wait poll loop, capped output capture); hand-written atomic writes (callisto-model/src/atomic.rs, callisto-manifests/src/atomic.rs; compare `tempfile::NamedTempFile::persist` and what the F_FULLFSYNC durability invariant in AGENTS.md requires); path/glob/semver/URL/TOML handling written by hand. Say for each whether a crate would delete code without losing a documented invariant, and name the crate; do NOT recommend new dependencies unless clearly worthwhile.\n4. Wildcard `_ =>` arms on our own enums where an exhaustive match would catch new variants (count and list the 10 riskiest, excluding the deliberate exit_kind() `_ => Runtime`).\n5. Public items never used outside their crate (`pub` that could be `pub(crate)`), using `cargo`-free analysis (grep) on callisto-graph and callisto-model; list the 15 largest.\nRefute your own candidates by reading c