d with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true; never gpgsign=false); no Claude-Session trailers or claude.ai links; one-line comments only for a non-obvious WHY; never hard-wrap prose. Verify by EXIT CODE: after committing run `sh /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/6cc3e47b/tmp/verify.sh .` with dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (five PASS lines). Push (`git push -u origin fix/python-requirement-idempotency`). No PR, no changeset (the caller decides).\nBUG: CI proptest `callisto-manifests python::tests::requirement_parse_render_parse_is_idempotent` (crates/callisto-manifests/src/python/tests.rs ~1639-1650) failed on input `s = \"¡[\\u{b}[\"` (U+00A1, `[`, vertical tab U+000B, `[`): first parse gives `Some(Requirement { name: \"¡\", extras: [], spec: None, marker: None })`, parsing its rendering gives `extras: [\"[\"]`. Proptest seed line: `cc 2c578f3eab22d4e06dc8df1cec7f86189896e013539f00ebf5b7525954de5126`. Find the parser/renderer (crates/callisto-manifests/src/python/ requirement parsing, `render`), reproduce with a deterministic unit test on that exact string FIRST (red), then fix the smallest way so parse -> render -> parse is idempotent: decide whether the parser should reject/normalise a stray `[` or whitespace-in-extras (vertical tab is whitespace for some checks and not others, `char::is_whitespace` vs ASCII), or the renderer should not emit something the parser reads differently. Prefer a fix where the parser and renderer share one definition (e.g. one whitespace/extras rule) over patching a symptom. Do not change behavior for valid PEP 508 requirements; run the existing python tests. Add the proptest regression line to crates/callisto-manifests/proptest-regressions/python/tests.txt (create if needed, same format as other regression files in the repo). Then run the proptest with a high case count once (e.g. PROPTEST_CASES=20000 cargo nextest run -p callisto-manifests requirement_parse_render) to look for sibling failures; if it finds more, fix the same root cause or report them.\nREPORT (under 200 words): root cause, the fix, red/green proof, whether the high-case run found more, commit signed?, five verify results.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8/tasks/afce7969e3192ad6f.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"07d346d2-b968-4910-85b8-dae630fce803","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","branch":"fix/drop-false-inference-alias","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a9b48a8c-9d51-41b7-a99d-ed474f8384f9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","sessionId":"6cc3e47b-8406-4c17-94fb-22313682fad8","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"fix/drop-false-inference-alias","slug":"mossy-snacking-stream"}
