{"parentUuid":"7b9259e6-26bb-458d-9141-d9e48b9733f6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b264255-fd5f-4477-ba2a-b23019e64de6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014nn5dc1SaqwBDhmvGRuXWa","type":"tool_result","content":"chore(release): version packages | DIRTY | updated 2026-11-11T22:44:20Z\n\n## Release Preview\n\nThis automated PR was generated by [Callisto](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto). Merging this PR will publish the updated packages to their release targets.\n\n### 📊 Release Summary\n\n| Package | Ecosystem | Current | Target | Bump | Reason |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `callisto-cli` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Changeset (`camel-case-json-fields`) |\n| `callisto-fixtures` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-graph` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-manifests` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-model` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **5 package(s)** queued for versioning. Minor bumps below 1.0.0 can include breaking changes, so read the changes below before merging.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Read before merging**\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that read `reason.dep_kind` or `reason.dependency_to` from `version` or `snapshot` JSON must use `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): keep Callisto and the release action on one version. A release preview or receipt written by 0.19 does not load in this version.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): if a group block in `callisto.toml` carries a key Callisto does not recognise, remove it.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that match E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that match E111 to detect an unknown key or a wrong-type value, or E171 to detect a bad `--from`, must match E325, E326, E327 or E328 instead.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): eight diagnostic codes that callisto no longer emits are gone from the JSON schema.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): a script that checks for exit code 1 after a bad argument must also accept 2. Checking for any non-zero code is unaffected.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): if a script checks for `command == \"release\"` on a failing `release pending`, match `release pending` instead.\n\n### 🚀 Merging will publish\n\n| Package | Goes to |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `callisto-model` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-manifests` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-graph` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-cli` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag · GitHub release · 5 assets |\n\nVersioned, not published: `callisto-fixtures` (no publish target).\n\n### 📦 What's Changing\n\n_Also bumped with no direct change of their own (released together via a fixed/linked group): `callisto-fixtures`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-model`._\n\n**15 change(s) across 5 package(s):**\n\n#### 🟡 Minor\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Every JSON field Callisto writes is now camelCase, so scripts see one naming style.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `version` and `snapshot` `--format json` reports: `reason.dep_kind` and `reason.dependency_to` are now `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n- Release plumbing files: the preview's `short_sha` is `shortSha`, and the receipt's `peeled_commit`, `tag_name` and `byte_length` are `peeledCommit`, `tagName` and `byteLength`.\n- A test now walks every report and file type and fails on a snake_case key.\n\nBreaking: scripts that read `reason.dep_kind` or `reason.dependency_to` from `version` or `snapshot` JSON must use `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n\nAction: keep Callisto and the release action on one version. A release preview or receipt written by 0.19 does not load in this version.\n\nPull request #498\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Mistyped config keys and pre-release tags are caught where you make them.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- An unknown key inside a `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` block now fails with an error naming the key. Before, it was silently ignored.\n- `callisto pre enter` rejects a tag with a space, `!`, `/`, an empty part or a number with a leading zero such as `01` (E324) and writes nothing. Before, it wrote `pre.json` and `version` failed later with a confusing version error. Dotted tags such as `beta.\n\nAction: if a group block in `callisto.toml` carries a key Callisto does not recognise, remove it.\n\nPull request #501\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Each configuration mistake now has its own error code, so a script or a person can tell them apart.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- E254 is retired. A bad `publish-to` is E330, `release-trigger` E331, `cascade.mode` E332, `changelog.layout` E333, a registry `kind` E334, `publish-url` on a non-PyPI registry E335, `url` on a Cargo registry E336, a registry timeout E337, and an unparsable p\n- A registry `kind` that does not match the package's ecosystem is E339. Before, it reported E171, which means an internal defect, so it looked like a bug in Callisto.\n- Exit codes are unchanged.\n\nBreaking: scripts that match E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes.\n\nPull request #506\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Error codes now each name one condition, so a script can tell problems apart from the code.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `callisto.toml`: E111 is only a TOML syntax error. An unknown key is E325, and a value of the wrong type or a missing required key is E326.\n- `release pending --from`: a value that is not a full 40-character SHA is E327, and a valid SHA that is not a release commit on this branch is E328. Before, both showed E171, which means an internal defect.\n\nBreaking: scripts that match E111 to detect an unknown key or a wrong-type value, or E171 to detect a bad `--from`, must match E325, E326, E327 or E328 instead.\n\nPull request #500\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Breaking: eight diagnostic codes that callisto no longer emits are gone from the JSON schema.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n**What changed**\n- `--format json` output never contains `napi-coordination-not-yet-supported`, `pre-major-inference-inert`, `changelog-section-not-found`, `changeset-read-error`, `git-discovery-failed`, `changelog-read-error`, `bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems` or `publi\n- The `DiagnosticCode` enum in the schema no longer lists them\n\n**Action**\n- Remove any match on these codes from scripts; a schema validator pinned to the old enum should be updated\n\nPull request #489\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>A private npm workspace root is no longer treated as a package.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- A root `package.json` that is `private` and lists `workspaces` is skipped, so it stops appearing in `status` and in release plans. Many project templates give that root a version such as `0.0.0`, and until now Callisto listed it as a package even though it o\n- `status` prints one line when it skips a root, so it never disappears silently.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4d52c771-1e03-4532-9f17-3ad18c8b8c3e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:49:51.440Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"chore(release): version packages | DIRTY | updated 2026-11-11T22:44:20Z\n\n## Release Preview\n\nThis automated PR was generated by [Callisto](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto). Merging this PR will publish the updated packages to their release targets.\n\n### 📊 Release Summary\n\n| Package | Ecosystem | Current | Target | Bump | Reason |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `callisto-cli` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Changeset (`camel-case-json-fields`) |\n| `callisto-fixtures` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-graph` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-manifests` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n| `callisto-model` | `cargo` | `0.19.0` | **`0.20.0`** | 🟡 `minor` | Fixed group `workspace` |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **5 package(s)** queued for versioning. Minor bumps below 1.0.0 can include breaking changes, so read the changes below before merging.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Read before merging**\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that read `reason.dep_kind` or `reason.dependency_to` from `version` or `snapshot` JSON must use `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): keep Callisto and the release action on one version. A release preview or receipt written by 0.19 does not load in this version.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): if a group block in `callisto.toml` carries a key Callisto does not recognise, remove it.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that match E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): scripts that match E111 to detect an unknown key or a wrong-type value, or E171 to detect a bad `--from`, must match E325, E326, E327 or E328 instead.\n> - **Breaking** (`callisto-cli`): eight diagnostic codes that callisto no longer emits are gone from the JSON schema.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): a script that checks for exit code 1 after a bad argument must also accept 2. Checking for any non-zero code is unaffected.\n> - **Action required** (`callisto-cli`): if a script checks for `command == \"release\"` on a failing `release pending`, match `release pending` instead.\n\n### 🚀 Merging will publish\n\n| Package | Goes to |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `callisto-model` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-manifests` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-graph` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag |\n| `callisto-cli` `0.20.0` | crates.io · git tag · GitHub release · 5 assets |\n\nVersioned, not published: `callisto-fixtures` (no publish target).\n\n### 📦 What's Changing\n\n_Also bumped with no direct change of their own (released together via a fixed/linked group): `callisto-fixtures`, `callisto-graph`, `callisto-manifests`, `callisto-model`._\n\n**15 change(s) across 5 package(s):**\n\n#### 🟡 Minor\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Every JSON field Callisto writes is now camelCase, so scripts see one naming style.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `version` and `snapshot` `--format json` reports: `reason.dep_kind` and `reason.dependency_to` are now `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n- Release plumbing files: the preview's `short_sha` is `shortSha`, and the receipt's `peeled_commit`, `tag_name` and `byte_length` are `peeledCommit`, `tagName` and `byteLength`.\n- A test now walks every report and file type and fails on a snake_case key.\n\nBreaking: scripts that read `reason.dep_kind` or `reason.dependency_to` from `version` or `snapshot` JSON must use `depKind` and `dependencyTo`.\n\nAction: keep Callisto and the release action on one version. A release preview or receipt written by 0.19 does not load in this version.\n\nPull request #498\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Mistyped config keys and pre-release tags are caught where you make them.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- An unknown key inside a `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` block now fails with an error naming the key. Before, it was silently ignored.\n- `callisto pre enter` rejects a tag with a space, `!`, `/`, an empty part or a number with a leading zero such as `01` (E324) and writes nothing. Before, it wrote `pre.json` and `version` failed later with a confusing version error. Dotted tags such as `beta.\n\nAction: if a group block in `callisto.toml` carries a key Callisto does not recognise, remove it.\n\nPull request #501\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Each configuration mistake now has its own error code, so a script or a person can tell them apart.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- E254 is retired. A bad `publish-to` is E330, `release-trigger` E331, `cascade.mode` E332, `changelog.layout` E333, a registry `kind` E334, `publish-url` on a non-PyPI registry E335, `url` on a Cargo registry E336, a registry timeout E337, and an unparsable p\n- A registry `kind` that does not match the package's ecosystem is E339. Before, it reported E171, which means an internal defect, so it looked like a bug in Callisto.\n- Exit codes are unchanged.\n\nBreaking: scripts that match E254 for these values, or E171 for a registry kind mismatch, must match the new codes.\n\nPull request #506\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Error codes now each name one condition, so a script can tell problems apart from the code.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- `callisto.toml`: E111 is only a TOML syntax error. An unknown key is E325, and a value of the wrong type or a missing required key is E326.\n- `release pending --from`: a value that is not a full 40-character SHA is E327, and a valid SHA that is not a release commit on this branch is E328. Before, both showed E171, which means an internal defect.\n\nBreaking: scripts that match E111 to detect an unknown key or a wrong-type value, or E171 to detect a bad `--from`, must match E325, E326, E327 or E328 instead.\n\nPull request #500\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Breaking: eight diagnostic codes that callisto no longer emits are gone from the JSON schema.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n**What changed**\n- `--format json` output never contains `napi-coordination-not-yet-supported`, `pre-major-inference-inert`, `changelog-section-not-found`, `changeset-read-error`, `git-discovery-failed`, `changelog-read-error`, `bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems` or `publi\n- The `DiagnosticCode` enum in the schema no longer lists them\n\n**Action**\n- Remove any match on these codes from scripts; a schema validator pinned to the old enum should be updated\n\nPull request #489\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>A private npm workspace root is no longer treated as a package.</b> — affects <code>callisto-cli</code></summary>\n\n- A root `package.json` that is `private` and lists `workspaces` is skipped, so it stops appearing in `status` and in release plans. Many project templates give that root a version such as `0.0.0`, and until now Callisto listed it as a package even though it o\n- `status` prints one line when it skips a root, so it never disappears silently.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a5812d0c-9c60-44b0-a95f-b6ca4597c304","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","branch":"fix/drop-false-inference-alias","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/drop-false-inference-alias","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7b9259e6-26bb-458d-9141-d9e48b9733f6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"se